## Business days — a measured gap in the toolchain, recorded not papered over

<!-- l4: decide:business days after -->

**55.** In relation to a DATE “the day” and a NUMBER “n”, business days after means if n is at most 0 then the day if is weekend with the day after with the day then business days after with the day after with the day and n otherwise business days after with the day after with the day and the difference between 1 and n.

<!-- l4: decide:rolled forward off a weekend -->

**56.** In relation to a DATE “the day”, rolled forward off a weekend means if is weekend with the day, then rolled forward off a weekend with the day after with the day; otherwise, the day.

## Annex — § 230.501(a), the accredited-investor test, at reduced surface

<!-- l4: declare:InvestorProfile -->

**57.** In this Act, “InvestorProfile” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “a natural person”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “within a category of § 230.501(a)(1)-(4) or (7)-(13) at the time of the sale, or reasonably believed to be”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “annual income for the calendar year”, being a NUMBER;

    (e) “annual income for the investor's own fiscal year”, being a NUMBER;

    (f) “revenue for the most recent fiscal year”, being a NUMBER;

    (g) “net assets as of the most recent fiscal year end”, being a NUMBER;

    (h) “total assets other than the primary residence”, being a NUMBER;

    (i) “total liabilities other than indebtedness secured by the primary residence”, being a NUMBER;

    (j) “estimated fair market value of the primary residence at the time of the sale”, being a NUMBER;

    (k) “indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding at the time of the sale”, being a NUMBER;

    (l) “indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding 60 days before the sale”, being a NUMBER;

    (m) “the increase in that indebtedness was the result of the acquisition of the primary residence”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “the purchase is made in accordance with a right to purchase such securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (o) “that right was held by the person on July 20, 2010”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (p) “qualified as an accredited investor on the basis of net worth at the time the right was acquired”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (q) “held securities of the same issuer, other than such right, on July 20, 2010”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (r) “net worth calculated without the paragraph (a)(5)(i) adjustments”, being a NUMBER;

    (s) “individual income in each of the two most recent years”, being a NUMBER;

    (t) “joint income with a spouse or spousal equivalent in each of those years”, being a NUMBER;

    (u) “a reasonable expectation of reaching the same income level in the current year”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (v) “aggregate amount of securities sold to the investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months”, being a NUMBER;

    (w) “annual income and net worth calculated jointly with that person's spouse”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (x) “the aggregate investment of the investor spouses”, being a NUMBER.

<!-- l4: decide:(C) — the indebtedness in excess of the fair market value -->

**58.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, (C) — the indebtedness in excess of the fair market value means max with 0 and the difference between investor's estimated fair market value of the primary residence at the time of the sale and investor's indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding at the time of the sale.

<!-- l4: decide:(B) — the increase in the indebtedness in the 60 days before the sale -->

**59.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, (B) — the increase in the indebtedness in the 60 days before the sale means if investor's the increase in that indebtedness was the result of the acquisition of the primary residence, then 0; otherwise, max with 0 and the difference between investor's indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding 60 days before the sale and investor's indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding at the time of the sale.

<!-- l4: decide:net worth computed under paragraph (a)(5)(i) -->

**60.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, net worth computed under paragraph (a)(5)(i) means the difference between (B) — the increase in the indebtedness in the 60 days before the sale with investor and the difference between (C) — the indebtedness in excess of the fair market value with investor and the difference between investor's total liabilities other than indebtedness secured by the primary residence and investor's total assets other than the primary residence.

<!-- l4: decide:paragraph (a)(5)(i) does not apply to this calculation -->

**61.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, paragraph (a)(5)(i) does not apply to this calculation if—

    (a) investor's the purchase is made in accordance with a right to purchase such securities;

    (b) (A);

    (c) investor's that right was held by the person on July 20, 2010;

    (d) (B);

    (e) investor's qualified as an accredited investor on the basis of net worth at the time the right was acquired;

    (f) (C); and

    (g) investor's held securities of the same issuer, other than such right, on July 20, 2010.

<!-- l4: decide:the investor's net worth -->

**62.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, the investor's net worth means if paragraph (a)(5)(i) does not apply to this calculation with investor, then investor's net worth calculated without the paragraph (a)(5)(i) adjustments; otherwise, net worth computed under paragraph (a)(5)(i) with investor.

<!-- l4: decide:(a)(5) — net worth exceeds one million dollars -->

**63.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, (a)(5) — net worth exceeds one million dollars if—

    (a) (5); and

    (b) the investor's net worth with investor is greater than the accredited investor net worth threshold.

<!-- l4: decide:(a)(6) — income in each of the two most recent years -->

**64.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, (a)(6) — income in each of the two most recent years if—

    (a) (6);

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) investor's individual income in each of the two most recent years is greater than the accredited investor individual income threshold; or

        (ii) investor's joint income with a spouse or spousal equivalent in each of those years is greater than the accredited investor joint income threshold; and

    (c) investor's a reasonable expectation of reaching the same income level in the current year.

<!-- l4: decide:the investor is an accredited investor -->

**65.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor”, the investor is an accredited investor if—

    (a) investor's within a category of § 230.501(a)(1)-(4) or (7)-(13) at the time of the sale, or reasonably believed to be;

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) (a)(5) — net worth exceeds one million dollars with investor; and

        (ii) investor's a natural person; or

    (c) all of the following apply—

        (i) (a)(6) — income in each of the two most recent years with investor; and

        (ii) investor's a natural person.

## Annex — § 270.3a-9, the crowdfunding vehicle

<!-- l4: declare:Crowdfunding vehicle -->

**66.** In this Act, “Crowdfunding vehicle” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “organized and operated for the sole purpose of directly acquiring, holding, and disposing of securities issued by a single crowdfunding issuer and raising capital in one or more Regulation Crowdfunding offerings”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “does not borrow money and uses the proceeds solely to purchase a single class of securities of a single crowdfunding issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “issues only one class of securities in offerings in which the vehicle and the crowdfunding issuer are deemed co-issuers”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “receives a written undertaking from the crowdfunding issuer to fund or reimburse its expenses, receives no other compensation, and any compensation paid to any person operating it is paid solely by the crowdfunding issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “maintains the same fiscal year-end as the crowdfunding issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “maintains a one-to-one relationship between the crowdfunding issuer securities it owns and its own securities outstanding”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “seeks instructions from the holders of its securities on voting and on tender or exchange offers, and acts only in accordance with those instructions”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “receives all Regulation Crowdfunding disclosures from the crowdfunding issuer and promptly provides them to its investors and to the relevant intermediary”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (j) “provides each investor the right to direct it to assert the rights the investor would have had if he or she had invested directly”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: decide:the vehicle is a crowdfunding vehicle deemed not to be an investment company -->

**67.** In relation to a Crowdfunding vehicle “vehicle”, the vehicle is a crowdfunding vehicle deemed not to be an investment company if—

    (a) (1);

    (b) vehicle's organized and operated for the sole purpose of directly acquiring, holding, and disposing of securities issued by a single crowdfunding issuer and raising capital in one or more Regulation Crowdfunding offerings;

    (c) (2);

    (d) vehicle's does not borrow money and uses the proceeds solely to purchase a single class of securities of a single crowdfunding issuer;

    (e) (3);

    (f) vehicle's issues only one class of securities in offerings in which the vehicle and the crowdfunding issuer are deemed co-issuers;

    (g) (4);

    (h) vehicle's receives a written undertaking from the crowdfunding issuer to fund or reimburse its expenses, receives no other compensation, and any compensation paid to any person operating it is paid solely by the crowdfunding issuer;

    (i) (5);

    (j) vehicle's maintains the same fiscal year-end as the crowdfunding issuer;

    (k) (6);

    (l) vehicle's maintains a one-to-one relationship between the crowdfunding issuer securities it owns and its own securities outstanding;

    (m) (7);

    (n) vehicle's seeks instructions from the holders of its securities on voting and on tender or exchange offers, and acts only in accordance with those instructions;

    (o) (8);

    (p) vehicle's receives all Regulation Crowdfunding disclosures from the crowdfunding issuer and promptly provides them to its investors and to the relevant intermediary;

    (q) (9); and

    (r) vehicle's provides each investor the right to direct it to assert the rights the investor would have had if he or she had invested directly.

## The facts — one record per thing the regulation asks a question about

<!-- l4: declare:Closing -->

**68.** In this Act, “Closing” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “date”, being a DATE; and

    (b) “amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6)”, being a NUMBER.

<!-- l4: declare:covered person class -->

**69.** In this Act, “covered person class” means one of the following—

    (a) “the issuer itself”;

    (b) “a predecessor of the issuer”;

    (c) “an affiliated issuer”;

    (d) “a director, officer, general partner or managing member of the issuer”;

    (e) “a beneficial owner of twenty percent or more of the issuer's outstanding voting equity securities”;

    (f) “a promoter connected with the issuer in any capacity”;

    (g) “a person paid remuneration for solicitation of purchasers”; or

    (h) “a general partner, director, officer or managing member of any such solicitor”.

<!-- l4: declare:CoveredPerson -->

**70.** In this Act, “CoveredPerson” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “class”, being a covered person class;

    (c) “convicted of a felony or misdemeanor in connection with the purchase or sale of any security”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “convicted of a felony or misdemeanor involving the making of a false filing with the Commission”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “convicted of a felony or misdemeanor arising out of the conduct of the business of an underwriter, broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser, funding portal or paid solicitor of purchasers of securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “date of the conviction”, being a DATE;

    (g) “subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct in connection with the purchase or sale of any security”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct involving the making of a false filing with the Commission”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct arising out of the conduct of the business of an underwriter, broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser, funding portal or paid solicitor of purchasers of securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “the court order, judgment or decree restrains or enjoins the person at the time of such filing or sale”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “date the court order, judgment or decree was entered”, being a DATE;

    (l) “subject to a final order of a State securities commission, a State bank or credit union supervisor, a State insurance commission, an appropriate Federal banking agency, the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission or the National Credit Union Administration”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (m) “that final order bars the person from association with an entity regulated by such commission, authority, agency or officer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “that final order bars the person from engaging in the business of securities, insurance or banking”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (o) “that final order bars the person from engaging in savings association or credit union activities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (p) “that final order is based on a violation of a law or regulation prohibiting fraudulent, manipulative or deceptive conduct”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (q) “date the final order was entered”, being a DATE;

    (r) “subject to an order of the Commission under section 15(b) or 15B(c) of the Exchange Act or section 203(e) or (f) of the Investment Advisers Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (s) “that Commission order suspends or revokes the person's registration as a broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser or funding portal”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (t) “that Commission order places limitations on the activities, functions or operations of the person”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (u) “that Commission order bars the person from being associated with any entity or from participating in the offering of any penny stock”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (v) “date the Commission order under section 15(b), 15B(c) or Advisers Act 203(e) or (f) was entered”, being a DATE;

    (w) “subject to a Commission order to cease and desist from committing or causing a violation of a scienter-based anti-fraud provision of the Federal securities laws”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (x) “subject to a Commission order to cease and desist from committing or causing a violation of section 5 of the Securities Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (y) “that cease-and-desist order is in effect at the time of such filing or sale”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (z) “date the Commission cease-and-desist order was entered”, being a DATE;

    (aa) “suspended or expelled from membership in, or suspended or barred from association with a member of, a registered national securities exchange or a registered national or affiliated securities association for conduct inconsistent with just and equitable principles of trade”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (bb) “date of the suspension or expulsion”, being a DATE;

    (cc) “filed as a registrant or issuer, or was named as an underwriter in, a registration statement or Regulation A offering statement that was the subject of a refusal order, stop order, or order suspending the Regulation A exemption”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (dd) “the subject, at the time of such filing or sale, of an investigation or proceeding to determine whether a stop order or suspension order should be issued”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (ee) “date of the refusal order, stop order or order suspending the Regulation A exemption”, being a DATE;

    (ff) “subject to a United States Postal Service false representation order”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (gg) “subject, at the time of such filing or sale, to a temporary restraining order or preliminary injunction with respect to conduct alleged by the United States Postal Service to constitute a scheme or device for obtaining money or property through the mail by means of false representations”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (hh) “date of the United States Postal Service false representation order”, being a DATE;

    (ii) “the court or regulatory authority that entered the relevant order, judgment or decree advised in writing that disqualification should not arise”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (jj) “the event occurred before the affiliation with the issuer arose”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (kk) “in control of the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (ll) “under common control with the issuer by a third party that was in control of the affiliated entity at the time of such events”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:IssuerProfile -->

**71.** In this Act, “IssuerProfile” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “organized under, and subject to, the laws of a State or territory of the United States or the District of Columbia”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “formerly subject to section 13 or 15(d) reporting, since terminated or suspended”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “an investment company as defined in section 3 of the Investment Company Act, or excluded from that definition by section 3(b) or section 3(c) of that Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “has filed with the Commission and provided to investors the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “no specific business plan, or a business plan to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentified company or companies”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “covered persons”, being a list of CoveredPerson;

    (j) “did not know and, in the exercise of reasonable care, could not have known that a disqualification existed”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “the Commission has determined that it is not necessary under the circumstances that an exemption be denied”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (l) “closings in reliance on section 4(a)(6)”, being a list of Closing;

    (m) “amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the 12-month period preceding the date of such offer or sale”, being a NUMBER;

    (n) “previously sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (o) “required to file reports under section 13(a) or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (p) “annual reports filed since its most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part”, being a NUMBER;

    (q) “holders of record”, being a NUMBER;

    (r) “investors who invested in the offering”, being a NUMBER;

    (s) “total assets”, being a NUMBER;

    (t) “all of the securities issued in reliance on section 4(a)(6) repurchased, including any payment in full of debt securities or any complete redemption of redeemable securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (u) “liquidated or dissolved its business in accordance with state law”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (v) “matters that would have triggered disqualification under § 227.503(a) but occurred before May 16, 2016”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (w) “those matters disclosed”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (x) “did not know and, in the exercise of reasonable care, could not have known of the existence of the undisclosed matter”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (y) “previously failed to comply with the ongoing reporting requirements of § 227.202”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (z) “date the offering statement was filed”, being a DATE; and

    (aa) “end of the fiscal year covered by the report”, being a DATE.

<!-- l4: declare:Disclosure -->

**72.** In this Act, “Disclosure” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “the name, legal status, physical address and Web site of the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “the names of the directors and officers, their positions, tenure and business experience during the past three years”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “the name of each beneficial owner of twenty percent or more of the issuer's outstanding voting equity securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “a description of the business of the issuer and the anticipated business plan of the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “the current number of employees of the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “a discussion of the material factors that make an investment in the issuer speculative or risky”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “the target offering amount and the deadline to reach the target offering amount”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “whether the issuer will accept investments in excess of the target offering amount and how oversubscriptions will be allocated”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “a description of the purpose and intended use of the offering proceeds”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “a description of the process to complete the transaction or cancel an investment commitment”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “a statement that an investor who does not reconfirm after a material change will have the commitment cancelled and the funds returned”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (l) “the price to the public of the securities or the method for determining the price”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (m) “a description of the ownership and capital structure of the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “the name, SEC file number and CRD number of the intermediary”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (o) “a description of the intermediary's financial interests in the issuer's transaction and in the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (p) “a description of the material terms of any indebtedness of the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (q) “a description of exempt offerings conducted within the past three years”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (r) “a description of related-party transactions above the five percent threshold”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (s) “a discussion of the issuer's financial condition”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (t) “the financial statements and tax information required by paragraph (t)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (u) “any matters that would have triggered disqualification under § 227.503(a) but occurred before May 16, 2016”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (v) “updates regarding the progress of the issuer in meeting the target offering amount”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (w) “where on the issuer's Web site investors will be able to find the issuer's annual report, and by when”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (x) “whether the issuer or any of its predecessors previously failed to comply with § 227.202”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (y) “any material information necessary to make the statements made not misleading”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (z) “any written communication or broadcast script provided in accordance with § 227.206 or § 230.241”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:OfferingProfile -->

**73.** In this Act, “OfferingProfile” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “target offering amount”, being a NUMBER;

    (b) “deadline identified in the issuer's offering materials”, being a DATE;

    (c) “the issuer will accept investments in excess of the target offering amount”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “maximum amount the issuer will accept”, being a NUMBER;

    (e) “date the § 227.201 and § 227.203(a) information was first made publicly available on the intermediary's platform”, being a DATE;

    (f) “sum of the investment commitments”, being a NUMBER;

    (g) “the offering statement filed prior to the commencement of the offering”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “the disclosure provided”, being a Disclosure;

    (i) “conducted through an intermediary that complies with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “conducted exclusively through the intermediary's platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “more than one intermediary used in this offering”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (l) “more than one intermediary used by the issuer for this capital raise”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (m) “the issuer complies with section 4A(b) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “the only failure to comply is with §§ 227.202, 227.203(a)(3) and 227.203(b)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (o) “the issuer knows that the investor has exceeded, or would exceed, the investor limits”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (p) “a material change to the terms of the offering or to the information provided by the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (q) “date the material change notice was received by the investor”, being a DATE;

    (r) “new offering deadline”, being a DATE;

    (s) “date the notice of the new offering deadline was provided”, being a DATE;

    (t) “notice given of the new, anticipated deadline of the offering”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (u) “notice given of the right of investors to cancel investment commitments for any reason until 48 hours prior to the new offering deadline”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (v) “notice given of whether the issuer will continue to accept investment commitments during the 48-hour period prior to the new offering deadline”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (w) “the issuer will continue to accept investment commitments during the 48-hour period prior to the new offering deadline”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (x) “the offering completed”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:CommitmentProfile -->

**74.** In this Act, “CommitmentProfile” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “investor”, being an InvestorProfile;

    (b) “amount of the investment commitment”, being a NUMBER;

    (c) “date the investment commitment was made”, being a DATE; and

    (d) “reconfirmed within five business days of receipt of the notice”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:IntermediaryProfile -->

**75.** In this Act, “IntermediaryProfile” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “registered with the Commission as a broker under section 15(b) of the Exchange Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “registered as a funding portal in accordance with § 227.400”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “a member of a national securities association registered under section 15A of the Exchange Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “a director, officer or partner of the intermediary has a financial interest in the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “the intermediary has a financial interest in the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “that financial interest received from the issuer as compensation for the services provided in connection with the offer or sale”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “that financial interest consists of securities of the same class and having the same terms, conditions and rights as the securities being offered”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “offers investment advice or recommendations”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “solicits purchases, sales or offers to buy the securities displayed on its platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “compensates employees, agents, or other persons for such solicitation or based on the sale of securities displayed or referenced on its platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (l) “holds, manages, possesses, or otherwise handles investor funds or securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (m) “a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer complies with section 4A(b) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer has established means to keep accurate records of the holders of the securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (o) “the issuer has engaged the services of a transfer agent registered under section 17A of the Exchange Act”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (p) “a reasonable basis for believing that a covered person is subject to a disqualification under § 227.503”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (q) “a background and securities enforcement regulatory history check conducted on the issuer and on each officer, director and twenty percent beneficial owner”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (r) “a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer or the offering presents the potential for fraud or otherwise raises concerns about investor protection”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (s) “unable to adequately or effectively assess the risk of fraud of the issuer or its potential offering”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (t) “became aware of that information after granting access”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (u) “the investor has opened an account with the intermediary”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (v) “the intermediary has obtained from the investor consent to electronic delivery of materials”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (w) “all subpart C information provided through electronic means”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (x) “the most current version of the educational materials available on its platform at all times”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (y) “a material revision made to the educational materials”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (z) “the revised educational materials made available to all investors before accepting any additional investment commitments”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (aa) “the investor informed about the promoter disclosure requirement”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (bb) “the manner in which the intermediary is compensated clearly disclosed”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (cc) “the issuer information made publicly available on its platform in a manner that reasonably permits a person to save, download, or otherwise store it”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (dd) “the issuer information remains publicly available until the offer and sale is completed or cancelled”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (ee) “no person required to establish an account with the intermediary to access that information”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (ff) “a reasonable basis for believing that the investor satisfies the investment limitations”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (gg) “a representation obtained that the investor has reviewed the educational materials, understands that the entire investment may be lost, and is in a financial condition to bear the loss”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (hh) “a questionnaire obtained demonstrating the investor's understanding of the restrictions on cancellation”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (ii) “a questionnaire obtained demonstrating the investor's understanding that it may be difficult to resell the securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (jj) “a questionnaire obtained demonstrating the investor's understanding that investing involves risk and that he or she should not invest funds he or she cannot afford to lose”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (kk) “communication channels provided on its platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (ll) “it does not participate in those communications other than to establish guidelines and remove abusive or potentially fraudulent communications”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (mm) “public access permitted to view the discussions in the communication channels”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (nn) “posting of comments restricted to persons who have opened an account”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (oo) “each person posting a comment required to disclose any promotional relationship with the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (pp) “makes publicly available on its platform frequent updates regarding the progress of the issuer in meeting the target offering amount”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (qq) “subject to a statutory disqualification as defined in section 3(a)(39) of the Exchange Act”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (rr) “so permitted pursuant to Commission rule or order”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:FundingPortalProfile -->

**76.** In this Act, “FundingPortalProfile” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “name”, being a STRING;

    (b) “a complete Form Funding Portal filed with the Commission”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “date the registration was received by the Commission”, being a DATE;

    (d) “date approved for membership by a registered national securities association”, being a DATE;

    (e) “nonresident”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “an information sharing arrangement in place between the Commission and the competent regulator”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “information previously submitted on Form Funding Portal has become inaccurate”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “date that information became inaccurate”, being a DATE;

    (i) “succeeds to and continues the business of a registered funding portal”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “the succession is based solely on a change of the predecessor's date or state of incorporation, form of organization, or composition of a partnership”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “date of the succession”, being a DATE;

    (l) “date the successor filed a registration on Form Funding Portal”, being a DATE;

    (m) “has ceased to operate as a funding portal”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “date the withdrawal was received by the Commission”, being a DATE;

    (o) “a longer period consented to by the funding portal or determined by the Commission by order”, being a DATE;

    (p) “a written consent and power of attorney appointing an agent in the United States obtained”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (q) “the name and address of its United States agent for service of process furnished on Schedule C”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (r) “a change of agent communicated promptly to the Commission through amendment of Schedule C”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (s) “a successor agent for service of process promptly appointed where required”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (t) “the written consent and power of attorney maintained as part of its books and records for at least three years after termination”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (u) “certified on Schedule C that it can and will provide prompt access to its books and records and submit to onsite inspection and examination”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (v) “an opinion of counsel provided that it can, as a matter of law, provide that access and submit to that inspection”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (w) “a change in the legal or regulatory framework affecting that access or inspection”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (x) “date of the change in the legal or regulatory framework”, being a DATE;

    (y) “written policies and procedures reasonably designed to achieve compliance with the federal securities laws implemented”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (z) “complies with the requirements of part 248 of this chapter as they apply to brokers”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (aa) “permits the examination and inspection of its business and business operations”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (bb) “the nine categories of records made and preserved for five years, the first two years in an easily accessible place”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (cc) “organizational documents made and preserved during the operation of the funding portal and of any successor”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (dd) “records produced, reproduced and maintained in the original, non-alterable format or as permitted under § 240.17a-4(f)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (ee) “a written undertaking filed with the registered national securities association where a third party maintains the records”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (ff) “records furnished promptly to the Commission and the association on request”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (gg) “subject to the requirements of the Currency and Foreign Transactions Reporting Act of 1970”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (hh) “the retention period required by 31 CFR chapter X in years”, being a NUMBER.

<!-- l4: declare:Transfer -->

**77.** In this Act, “Transfer” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “date the securities were issued in a transaction exempt under section 4(a)(6)”, being a DATE;

    (b) “date of the transfer”, being a DATE;

    (c) “to the issuer of the securities”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “to an accredited investor”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “as part of an offering registered with the Commission”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (f) “to a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent, to a trust controlled by the purchaser, to a trust created for the benefit of such a family member, or in connection with the death or divorce of the purchaser or other similar circumstance”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:Communication -->

**78.** In this Act, “Communication” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “directs investors to the intermediary's platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “includes no more than the information specified in § 227.204(b)(1) through (3)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “made through communication channels provided by an intermediary on the intermediary's platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “the issuer identifies itself as the issuer in the communication”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “a person acting on behalf of the issuer identifies that affiliation in the communication”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “states that no money or other consideration is being solicited, and if sent in response, will not be accepted”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “states that no offer to buy the securities can be accepted and no part of the purchase price can be received until the offering statement is filed and only through an intermediary's platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “states that a person's indication of interest involves no obligation or commitment of any kind”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “clearly discloses the receipt, past or prospective, of compensation with the communication”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (j) “made before the filing of the offering statement”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:DeviationClaim -->

**79.** In this Act, “DeviationClaim” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “a failure to comply with a term, condition, or requirement of this part”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “the failure to comply was insignificant with respect to the offering as a whole”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “the issuer made a good faith and reasonable attempt to comply with all applicable terms, conditions and requirements of this part”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “the failure resulted from the intermediary's failure to comply with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related rules”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “the issuer did not know of such failure”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (f) “the intermediary's failure occurred solely in offerings other than the issuer's offering”, being a BOOLEAN.

## § 227.503 Disqualification provisions

<!-- l4: decide:the date that many years earlier -->

**80.** In relation to a DATE “the anchor” and a NUMBER “years”, the date that many years earlier means Date with DATE_DAY with the anchor, DATE_MONTH with the anchor and the difference between years and DATE_YEAR with the anchor.

<!-- l4: decide:falls within the lookback of -->

**81.** In relation to a DATE “the event”, a DATE “the anchor” and a NUMBER “years”, falls within the lookback of means the event is at least the date that many years earlier with the anchor and years.

<!-- l4: decide:not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) -->

**82.** In relation to a DATE “the event”, not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) means the event is at least the disqualification transition date.

<!-- l4: decide:the conviction lookback in years -->

**83.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person”, the conviction lookback in years means consider the case distinctions of person's class :  when the issuer itself has  then the five year disqualification lookback. when a predecessor of the issuer has  then the five year disqualification lookback. when an affiliated issuer has  then the five year disqualification lookback. in any other case the ten year disqualification lookback.

<!-- l4: decide:the conviction is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii) -->

**84.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person”, the conviction is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii) if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) (i); and

        (ii) person's convicted of a felony or misdemeanor in connection with the purchase or sale of any security;

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) (ii); and

        (ii) person's convicted of a felony or misdemeanor involving the making of a false filing with the Commission; or

    (c) all of the following apply—

        (i) (iii); and

        (ii) person's convicted of a felony or misdemeanor arising out of the conduct of the business of an underwriter, broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser, funding portal or paid solicitor of purchasers of securities.

<!-- l4: decide:503(a)(1) — a disqualifying conviction -->

**85.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, 503(a)(1) — a disqualifying conviction if—

    (a) (1);

    (b) the conviction is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii) with person;

    (c) falls within the lookback of with person's date of the conviction, the filing and the conviction lookback in years with person; and

    (d) not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) with person's date of the conviction.

<!-- l4: decide:the court order is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii) -->

**86.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person”, the court order is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii) if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) (i); and

        (ii) person's subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct in connection with the purchase or sale of any security;

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) (ii); and

        (ii) person's subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct involving the making of a false filing with the Commission; or

    (c) all of the following apply—

        (i) (iii); and

        (ii) person's subject to a court order, judgment or decree restraining or enjoining conduct arising out of the conduct of the business of an underwriter, broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser, funding portal or paid solicitor of purchasers of securities.

<!-- l4: decide:503(a)(2) — a court order restraining or enjoining -->

**87.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, 503(a)(2) — a court order restraining or enjoining if—

    (a) (2);

    (b) the court order is of a kind described in (i), (ii) or (iii) with person;

    (c) person's the court order, judgment or decree restrains or enjoins the person at the time of such filing or sale;

    (d) falls within the lookback of with person's date the court order, judgment or decree was entered, the filing and the five year disqualification lookback; and

    (e) not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) with person's date the court order, judgment or decree was entered.

<!-- l4: decide:the final order bars the person as described in (A), (B) or (C) -->

**88.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person”, the final order bars the person as described in (A), (B) or (C) if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) (A); and

        (ii) person's that final order bars the person from association with an entity regulated by such commission, authority, agency or officer;

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) (B); and

        (ii) person's that final order bars the person from engaging in the business of securities, insurance or banking; or

    (c) all of the following apply—

        (i) (C); and

        (ii) person's that final order bars the person from engaging in savings association or credit union activities.

<!-- l4: decide:the final order is a fraud-based order within ten years -->

**89.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, the final order is a fraud-based order within ten years if—

    (a) (ii);

    (b) person's that final order is based on a violation of a law or regulation prohibiting fraudulent, manipulative or deceptive conduct; and

    (c) falls within the lookback of with person's date the final order was entered, the filing and the ten year disqualification lookback.

<!-- l4: decide:503(a)(3) — a final order of a State or Federal regulator -->

**90.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, 503(a)(3) — a final order of a State or Federal regulator if—

    (a) (3);

    (b) person's subject to a final order of a State securities commission, a State bank or credit union supervisor, a State insurance commission, an appropriate Federal banking agency, the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission or the National Credit Union Administration;

    (c) any of the following applies—

        (i) all of the following apply—

            (A) (i); and

            (B) the final order bars the person as described in (A), (B) or (C) with person; or

        (ii) the final order is a fraud-based order within ten years with person and the filing; and

    (d) not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) with person's date the final order was entered.

<!-- l4: decide:the Commission order does what (i), (ii) or (iii) describes -->

**91.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person”, the Commission order does what (i), (ii) or (iii) describes if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) (i); and

        (ii) person's that Commission order suspends or revokes the person's registration as a broker, dealer, municipal securities dealer, investment adviser or funding portal;

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) (ii); and

        (ii) person's that Commission order places limitations on the activities, functions or operations of the person; or

    (c) all of the following apply—

        (i) (iii); and

        (ii) person's that Commission order bars the person from being associated with any entity or from participating in the offering of any penny stock.

<!-- l4: decide:503(a)(4) — a Commission registration order -->

**92.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person”, 503(a)(4) — a Commission registration order if—

    (a) (4);

    (b) person's subject to an order of the Commission under section 15(b) or 15B(c) of the Exchange Act or section 203(e) or (f) of the Investment Advisers Act;

    (c) the Commission order does what (i), (ii) or (iii) describes with person; and

    (d) not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) with person's date the Commission order under section 15(b), 15B(c) or Advisers Act 203(e) or (f) was entered.

<!-- l4: decide:the cease-and-desist order is of a kind described in (i) or (ii) -->

**93.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person”, the cease-and-desist order is of a kind described in (i) or (ii) if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) (i); and

        (ii) person's subject to a Commission order to cease and desist from committing or causing a violation of a scienter-based anti-fraud provision of the Federal securities laws; or

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) (ii); and

        (ii) person's subject to a Commission order to cease and desist from committing or causing a violation of section 5 of the Securities Act.

<!-- l4: decide:503(a)(5) — a Commission cease-and-desist order -->

**94.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, 503(a)(5) — a Commission cease-and-desist order if—

    (a) (5);

    (b) the cease-and-desist order is of a kind described in (i) or (ii) with person;

    (c) person's that cease-and-desist order is in effect at the time of such filing or sale;

    (d) falls within the lookback of with person's date the Commission cease-and-desist order was entered, the filing and the five year disqualification lookback; and

    (e) not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) with person's date the Commission cease-and-desist order was entered.

<!-- l4: decide:503(a)(6) — suspension or expulsion by a self-regulatory organisation -->

**95.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person”, 503(a)(6) — suspension or expulsion by a self-regulatory organisation if—

    (a) (6);

    (b) person's suspended or expelled from membership in, or suspended or barred from association with a member of, a registered national securities exchange or a registered national or affiliated securities association for conduct inconsistent with just and equitable principles of trade; and

    (c) not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) with person's date of the suspension or expulsion.

<!-- l4: decide:503(a)(7) — a refused, stopped or suspended registration or Regulation A statement -->

**96.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, 503(a)(7) — a refused, stopped or suspended registration or Regulation A statement if—

    (a) (7);

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) all of the following apply—

            (A) person's filed as a registrant or issuer, or was named as an underwriter in, a registration statement or Regulation A offering statement that was the subject of a refusal order, stop order, or order suspending the Regulation A exemption; and

            (B) falls within the lookback of with person's date of the refusal order, stop order or order suspending the Regulation A exemption, the filing and the five year disqualification lookback; or

        (ii) person's the subject, at the time of such filing or sale, of an investigation or proceeding to determine whether a stop order or suspension order should be issued; and

    (c) not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) with person's date of the refusal order, stop order or order suspending the Regulation A exemption.

<!-- l4: decide:503(a)(8) — a Postal Service false representation order -->

**97.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, 503(a)(8) — a Postal Service false representation order if—

    (a) (8);

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) all of the following apply—

            (A) person's subject to a United States Postal Service false representation order; and

            (B) falls within the lookback of with person's date of the United States Postal Service false representation order, the filing and the five year disqualification lookback; or

        (ii) person's subject, at the time of such filing or sale, to a temporary restraining order or preliminary injunction with respect to conduct alleged by the United States Postal Service to constitute a scheme or device for obtaining money or property through the mail by means of false representations; and

    (c) not caught by the transition in paragraph (b)(1) with person's date of the United States Postal Service false representation order.

<!-- l4: decide:503(c) — the event is excused as a pre-affiliation event of an affiliated issuer -->

**98.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person”, 503(c) — the event is excused as a pre-affiliation event of an affiliated issuer if—

    (a) person's class is equal to an affiliated issuer;

    (b) person's the event occurred before the affiliation with the issuer arose; and

    (c) none of the following applies—

        (i) all of the following apply—

            (A) (1); and

            (B) person's in control of the issuer; or

        (ii) all of the following apply—

            (A) (2); and

            (B) person's under common control with the issuer by a third party that was in control of the affiliated entity at the time of such events.

<!-- l4: decide:a disqualifying event has occurred with respect to the covered person -->

**99.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, a disqualifying event has occurred with respect to the covered person if—

    (a) 503(a)(1) — a disqualifying conviction with person and the filing;

    (b) 503(a)(2) — a court order restraining or enjoining with person and the filing;

    (c) 503(a)(3) — a final order of a State or Federal regulator with person and the filing;

    (d) 503(a)(4) — a Commission registration order with person;

    (e) 503(a)(5) — a Commission cease-and-desist order with person and the filing;

    (f) 503(a)(6) — suspension or expulsion by a self-regulatory organisation with person;

    (g) 503(a)(7) — a refused, stopped or suspended registration or Regulation A statement with person and the filing; or

    (h) 503(a)(8) — a Postal Service false representation order with person and the filing.

<!-- l4: decide:the covered person is disqualified -->

**100.** In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, the covered person is disqualified if—

    (a) a disqualifying event has occurred with respect to the covered person with person and the filing;

    (b) it is not the case that—

        (i) (3); and

        (ii) person's the court or regulatory authority that entered the relevant order, judgment or decree advised in writing that disqualification should not arise; and

    (c) 503(c) — the event is not excused as a pre-affiliation event of an affiliated issuer with person.

<!-- l4: decide:no exemption is available because of a disqualification -->

**101.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, no exemption is available because of a disqualification if—

    (a) any with is disqualified at the filing date and issuer's covered persons;

    (b) it is not the case that—

        (i) (2); and

        (ii) issuer's the Commission has determined that it is not necessary under the circumstances that an exemption be denied; and

    (c) it is not the case that—

        (i) (4); and

        (ii) issuer's did not know and, in the exercise of reasonable care, could not have known that a disqualification existed.

For the purposes of this provision—

“is disqualified at the filing date” means the covered person is disqualified with person and issuer's date the offering statement was filed;

<!-- l4: decide:the person may not act as or for an intermediary -->

**102.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the person may not act as or for an intermediary if—

