## § 227.501 Restrictions on resales

<!-- l4: decide:the first anniversary of the issuance -->

**103.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, the first anniversary of the issuance means Date with DATE_DAY with transfer's date the securities were issued in a transaction exempt under section 4(a)(6), DATE_MONTH with transfer's date the securities were issued in a transaction exempt under section 4(a)(6) and the sum of DATE_YEAR with transfer's date the securities were issued in a transaction exempt under section 4(a)(6) and the resale restriction in years.

<!-- l4: decide:the transfer falls within the one-year restricted period -->

**104.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, the transfer falls within the one-year restricted period means transfer's date of the transfer is less than the first anniversary of the issuance with transfer.

<!-- l4: decide:the transfer falls within an exception in § 227.501(a) -->

**105.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, the transfer falls within an exception in § 227.501(a) if—

    (a) unless such securities are transferred:;

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) (1); and

        (ii) transfer's to the issuer of the securities;

    (c) all of the following apply—

        (i) (2); and

        (ii) transfer's to an accredited investor;

    (d) all of the following apply—

        (i) (3); and

        (ii) transfer's as part of an offering registered with the Commission; or

    (e) all of the following apply—

        (i) (4); and

        (ii) transfer's to a member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent, to a trust controlled by the purchaser, to a trust created for the benefit of such a family member, or in connection with the death or divorce of the purchaser or other similar circumstance.

<!-- l4: decide:the transfer is permitted -->

**106.** In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, the transfer is permitted if—

    (a) it is not the case that the transfer falls within the one-year restricted period with transfer; or

    (b) the transfer falls within an exception in § 227.501(a) with transfer.

<!-- l4: decide:the meaning of "member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent" -->

**107.** The meaning of "member of the family of the purchaser or the equivalent" if—

    (a) includes a child, stepchild, grandchild, parent, stepparent, grandparent, spouse or spousal equivalent, sibling, mother-in-law, father-in-law, son-in-law, daughter-in-law, brother-in-law, or sister-in-law of the purchaser, and shall include adoptive relationships.;

    (b) The term spousal equivalent means a cohabitant occupying a relationship generally equivalent to that of a spouse.; and

    (c) TRUE.

## § 227.504 Definition of "qualified purchaser"

<!-- l4: decide:a person to whom securities are offered or sold under this part is a qualified purchaser -->

**108.** A person to whom securities are offered or sold under this part is a qualified purchaser if—

    (a) For purposes of section 18(b)(3) of the Securities Act [15 U.S.C. 77r(b)(3)], a "qualified purchaser" means any person to whom securities are offered or sold pursuant to an offering under §§ 227.100 through 227.504 (Regulation Crowdfunding).; and

    (b) TRUE.

## § 227.100 Crowdfunding exemption and requirements

<!-- l4: decide:amount sold in the twelve months running from each closing -->

**109.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer” and a DATE “the date of the offer or sale”, amount sold in the twelve months running from each closing means sum with map with the amount of the closing and filter with the closing's twelve-month anniversary has not passed and issuer's closings in reliance on section 4(a)(6).

For the purposes of this provision—

“the window opens” means the date that many years earlier with the date of the offer or sale and 1;

“the closing's twelve-month anniversary has not passed” means c's date is at least the window opens;

“the amount of the closing” means c's amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6);

<!-- l4: decide:the amount already sold in the twelve month window -->

**110.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an IssuerProfile “issuer” and a DATE “the date of the offer or sale”, the amount already sold in the twelve month window means consider the case distinctions of interp's twelve month window anchor :  when rolling from each closing has  then amount sold in the twelve months running from each closing with issuer and the date of the offer or sale. when from the date of such offer or sale has  then issuer's amount sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the 12-month period preceding the date of such offer or sale.

<!-- l4: decide:the amount attributable to this transaction -->

**111.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, the amount attributable to this transaction means if offering's the issuer will accept investments in excess of the target offering amount, then offering's maximum amount the issuer will accept; otherwise, offering's target offering amount.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's headroom under the twelve month cap -->

**112.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an IssuerProfile “issuer”, an OfferingProfile “offering” and a DATE “the date of the offer or sale”, the issuer's headroom under the twelve month cap means the difference between the amount already sold in the twelve month window with interp, issuer and the date of the offer or sale and the aggregate offering cap.

<!-- l4: decide:100(a)(1) — the aggregate amount does not exceed the cap -->

**113.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an IssuerProfile “issuer”, an OfferingProfile “offering” and a DATE “the date of the offer or sale”, 100(a)(1) — the aggregate amount does not exceed the cap if—

    (a) (1); and

    (b) the sum of the amount already sold in the twelve month window with interp, issuer and the date of the offer or sale and the amount attributable to this transaction with offering is at most the aggregate offering cap.

<!-- l4: decide:the investor's annual income -->

**114.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an InvestorProfile “investor”, the investor's annual income means consider the case distinctions of interp's annual income period :  when the calendar year has  then investor's annual income for the calendar year. when the investor's own fiscal year has  then investor's annual income for the investor's own fiscal year.

<!-- l4: decide:the first of the investor's two measured quantities -->

**115.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an InvestorProfile “investor”, the first of the investor's two measured quantities means if investor's a natural person, then the investor's annual income with interp and investor; otherwise, consider the case distinctions of interp's non-natural investor limit basis :  when revenue or net assets has  then investor's revenue for the most recent fiscal year. when annual income or net worth has  then the investor's annual income with interp and investor.

<!-- l4: decide:the second of the investor's two measured quantities -->

**116.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an InvestorProfile “investor”, the second of the investor's two measured quantities means if investor's a natural person, then the investor's net worth with investor; otherwise, consider the case distinctions of interp's non-natural investor limit basis :  when revenue or net assets has  then investor's net assets as of the most recent fiscal year end. when annual income or net worth has  then the investor's net worth with investor.

<!-- l4: decide:the greater of the investor's two measured quantities -->

**117.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an InvestorProfile “investor”, the greater of the investor's two measured quantities means max with the first of the investor's two measured quantities with interp and investor and the second of the investor's two measured quantities with interp and investor.

<!-- l4: decide:both measured quantities are at or above the tier boundary -->

**118.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an InvestorProfile “investor”, both measured quantities are at or above the tier boundary if—

    (a) the first of the investor's two measured quantities with interp and investor is at least the investor tier boundary; and

    (b) the second of the investor's two measured quantities with interp and investor is at least the investor tier boundary.

<!-- l4: decide:the investment limit for the investor -->

**119.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an InvestorProfile “investor”, the investment limit for the investor means if both measured quantities are at or above the tier boundary with interp and investor then min with the result of dividing the product of the greater of the investor's two measured quantities with interp and investor and the upper investment limit rate percent by 100 and the investor ceiling otherwise max with the investor floor and the result of dividing the product of the greater of the investor's two measured quantities with interp and investor and the lower investment limit rate percent by 100.

<!-- l4: decide:the amount tested against the investor's limit -->

**120.** In relation to an InvestorProfile “investor” and a NUMBER “this investment”, the amount tested against the investor's limit means if investor's annual income and net worth calculated jointly with that person's spouse, then the sum of investor's the aggregate investment of the investor spouses and this investment; otherwise, the sum of investor's aggregate amount of securities sold to the investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months and this investment.

<!-- l4: decide:100(a)(2) — the investor's limit is not exceeded -->

**121.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an InvestorProfile “investor” and a NUMBER “this investment”, 100(a)(2) — the investor's limit is not exceeded if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) (2); and

        (ii) the investor is an accredited investor with investor; or

    (b) the amount tested against the investor's limit with investor and this investment is at most the investment limit for the investor with interp and investor.

<!-- l4: decide:100(a)(2) — satisfied, or within the intermediary-reliance safe harbour -->

**122.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an InvestorProfile “investor”, an OfferingProfile “offering” and a NUMBER “this investment”, 100(a)(2) — satisfied, or within the intermediary-reliance safe harbour if—

    (a) 100(a)(2) — the investor's limit is not exceeded with interp, investor and this investment; or

    (b) offering's the issuer knows that the investor does not have exceeded, or would exceed, the investor limits.

<!-- l4: decide:more than one intermediary has been used -->

**123.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an OfferingProfile “offering”, more than one intermediary has been used means consider the case distinctions of interp's one intermediary scope :  when the prohibition binds the offering has  then offering's more than one intermediary used in this offering. when the prohibition binds the issuer has  then offering's more than one intermediary used by the issuer for this capital raise.

<!-- l4: decide:100(a)(3) — conducted through one compliant intermediary, exclusively -->

**124.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an OfferingProfile “offering”, 100(a)(3) — conducted through one compliant intermediary, exclusively if—

    (a) (3);

    (b) offering's conducted through an intermediary that complies with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part;

    (c) offering's conducted exclusively through the intermediary's platform; and

    (d) more than one intermediary does not have been used with interp and offering.

<!-- l4: decide:100(a)(4) — the issuer complies with section 4A(b) -->

**125.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, 100(a)(4) — the issuer complies with section 4A(b) if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) (4); and

        (ii) offering's the issuer complies with section 4A(b) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part; or

    (b) offering's the only failure to comply is with §§ 227.202, 227.203(a)(3) and 227.203(b).

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer is caught by the Exchange Act reporting limb -->

**126.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an IssuerProfile “issuer”, the issuer is caught by the Exchange Act reporting limb means consider the case distinctions of interp's reporting disqualification tense :  when presently subject to the reporting requirement has  then issuer's subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act. when ever subject to the reporting requirement has  then issuer's subject to the requirement to file reports pursuant to section 13 or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act or issuer's formerly subject to section 13 or 15(d) reporting, since terminated or suspended.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer is delinquent in its ongoing reports -->

**127.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, the issuer is delinquent in its ongoing reports if—

    (a) issuer's has sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6); and

    (b) issuer's does not have filed with the Commission and provided to investors the ongoing annual reports required during the two years immediately preceding the filing of the offering statement.

<!-- l4: decide:100(b)(7) — reserved -->

**128.** 100(b)(7) — reserved if—

    (a) (7) [Reserved];

    (b) [the paragraph carried a COVID-era expedited offering route from 2021-01-14 until it lapsed on 2023-03-01; that text is not in this bundle and is deliberately not reproduced]; and

    (c) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the crowdfunding exemption does not apply to the issuer -->

**129.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an IssuerProfile “issuer”, the crowdfunding exemption does not apply to the issuer if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

