<!-- l4: decide:the extended meaning of "issuer" in § 227.100(c) -->

**130.** The extended meaning of "issuer" in § 227.100(c) if—

    (a) For purposes of § 227.201(r), calculating aggregate amounts offered and sold in § 227.100(a) and § 227.201(t), and determining whether an issuer has previously sold securities in § 227.201(t)(3), issuer includes all entities controlled by or under common control with the issuer and any predecessors of the issuer.;

    (b) The term control means the possession, direct or indirect, of the power to direct or cause the direction of the management and policies of the entity, whether through the ownership of voting securities, by contract or otherwise.; and

    (c) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the meaning of "investor" in § 227.100(d) -->

**131.** The meaning of "investor" in § 227.100(d) if—

    (a) For purposes of this part, investor means any investor or any potential investor, as the context requires.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the crowdfunding vehicle is not considered an investor for the purposes of this part -->

**132.** In relation to a Crowdfunding vehicle “vehicle”, the crowdfunding vehicle is not considered an investor for the purposes of this part means the vehicle is a crowdfunding vehicle deemed not to be an investment company with vehicle.

<!-- l4: decide:integration with other offerings -->

**133.** Integration with other offerings if—

    (a) To determine whether offers and sales should be integrated, see § 230.152 of this chapter.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the crowdfunding exemption is available -->

**134.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an IssuerProfile “issuer”, an OfferingProfile “offering”, an InvestorProfile “investor”, a NUMBER “this investment” and a DATE “the date of the offer or sale”, the crowdfunding exemption is available if—

    (a) (a) An issuer may offer or sell securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act, provided that:;

    (b) 100(a)(1) — the aggregate amount does not exceed the cap with interp, issuer, offering and the date of the offer or sale;

    (c) 100(a)(2) — satisfied, or within the intermediary-reliance safe harbour with interp, investor, offering and this investment;

    (d) 100(a)(3) — conducted through one compliant intermediary, exclusively with interp and offering;

    (e) 100(a)(4) — the issuer complies with section 4A(b) with offering; and

    (f) it is not the case that the crowdfunding exemption does not apply to the issuer with interp and issuer.

## The regulative vocabulary — who acts, and what the acts are

<!-- l4: declare:Reg CF party -->

**135.** In this Act, “Reg CF party” means one of the following—

    (a) “the issuer”;

    (b) “the intermediary”;

    (c) “the funding portal”;

    (d) “the investor”; or

    (e) “the qualified third party”.

<!-- l4: declare:Reg CF act -->

**136.** In this Act, “Reg CF act” means one of the following—

    (a) “file with the Commission and provide to investors and the relevant intermediary the information required by § 227.201”;

    (b) “file with the Commission and post on the issuer's Web site an annual report”;

    (c) “file a Form C offering statement”;

    (d) “file a Form C/A amendment to the offering statement”;

    (e) “file a Form C-U progress update”;

    (f) “file a final Form C-U disclosing the total amount of securities sold”;

    (g) “file a Form C-AR annual report”;

    (h) “file a Form C-AR/A amendment to the annual report”;

    (i) “file a Form C-TR termination of reporting”;

    (j) “advertise the terms of the offering”;

    (k) “communicate with investors through the intermediary's communication channels”;

    (l) “compensate a person to promote the issuer's offerings”;

    (m) “solicit or accept money, other consideration, or a commitment”;

    (n) “communicate to determine whether there is any interest in a contemplated securities offering”;

    (o) “deny access to its platform to the issuer”;

    (p) “remove the offering from its platform, cancel the offering, and return the funds committed by investors”;

    (q) “accept an investment commitment”;

    (r) “deliver the educational materials to the investor”;

    (s) “make the issuer information publicly available on its platform”;

    (t) “give or send the investor notice of the investment commitment”;

    (u) “give or send the investor notice of the material change”;

    (v) “give or send the investor notice of the cancellation and the refund amount”;

    (w) “direct the refund of investor funds”;

    (x) “prevent investors from making investment commitments with respect to that offering”;

    (y) “direct the qualified third party to transmit the funds to the issuer”;

    (z) “give or send the investor confirmation of the transaction”;

    (aa) “compensate a person for the personally identifiable information of an investor”;

    (bb) “reconfirm the investment commitment”;

    (cc) “cancel the investment commitment”;

    (dd) “register on Form Funding Portal and become a member of a national securities association”;

    (ee) “file an amendment to Form Funding Portal”;

    (ff) “file a withdrawal of registration on Form Funding Portal”;

    (gg) “re-certify on Schedule C to Form Funding Portal”;

    (hh) “make and preserve the records required by § 227.404”; or

    (ii) “permit the examination and inspection of its business and business operations”.

## § 227.201 Disclosure requirements

