    (w) (l);

    (x) offering's the disclosure provided's the price to the public of the securities or the method for determining the price;

    (y) (m);

    (z) offering's the disclosure provided's a description of the ownership and capital structure of the issuer;

    (aa) (n);

    (bb) offering's the disclosure provided's the name, SEC file number and CRD number of the intermediary;

    (cc) (o);

    (dd) offering's the disclosure provided's a description of the intermediary's financial interests in the issuer's transaction and in the issuer;

    (ee) (p);

    (ff) offering's the disclosure provided's a description of the material terms of any indebtedness of the issuer;

    (gg) (q);

    (hh) offering's the disclosure provided's a description of exempt offerings conducted within the past three years;

    (ii) (r);

    (jj) offering's the disclosure provided's a description of related-party transactions above the five percent threshold;

    (kk) (s);

    (ll) offering's the disclosure provided's a discussion of the issuer's financial condition;

    (mm) (t);

    (nn) offering's the disclosure provided's the financial statements and tax information required by paragraph (t);

    (oo) (u);

    (pp) offering's the disclosure provided's any matters that would have triggered disqualification under § 227.503(a) but occurred before May 16, 2016;

    (qq) (v);

    (rr) offering's the disclosure provided's updates regarding the progress of the issuer in meeting the target offering amount;

    (ss) (w);

    (tt) offering's the disclosure provided's where on the issuer's Web site investors will be able to find the issuer's annual report, and by when;

    (uu) (x);

    (vv) offering's the disclosure provided's whether the issuer or any of its predecessors previously failed to comply with § 227.202;

    (ww) (y);

    (xx) offering's the disclosure provided's any material information necessary to make the statements made not misleading;

    (yy) (z); and

    (zz) offering's the disclosure provided's any written communication or broadcast script provided in accordance with § 227.206 or § 230.241.

<!-- l4: decide:201(aa) — reserved -->

**138.** 201(aa) — reserved if—

    (a) (aa) [Reserved]; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the instruction to § 227.201 on cross-references -->

**139.** The instruction to § 227.201 on cross-references if—

    (a) If disclosure provided pursuant to any paragraph of this section also satisfies the requirements of one or more other paragraphs of this section, it is not necessary to repeat the disclosure. Instead of repeating information, an issuer may include a cross-reference to disclosure contained elsewhere in the offering statement or report, including to information in the financial statements.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: declare:financial statement requirement -->

**140.** In this Act, “financial statement requirement” means one of the following—

    (a) “tax return information with financial statements certified by the principal executive officer”;

    (b) “financial statements reviewed by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer”; or

    (c) “financial statements audited by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer”.

<!-- l4: decide:the aggregate target offering amount for § 227.201(t) -->

**141.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an IssuerProfile “issuer” and an OfferingProfile “offering”, the aggregate target offering amount for § 227.201(t) means the sum of the amount already sold in the twelve month window with interp, issuer and issuer's date the offering statement was filed and the amount attributable to this transaction with offering.

<!-- l4: decide:the financial statements required -->

**142.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an IssuerProfile “issuer” and an OfferingProfile “offering”, the financial statements required means if the aggregate target offering amount for § 227.201(t) with interp, issuer and offering is at most the tax return information ceiling then tax return information with financial statements certified by the principal executive officer if the aggregate target offering amount for § 227.201(t) with interp, issuer and offering is at most the reviewed statements ceiling then financial statements reviewed by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer if not issuer's previously sold securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) and the aggregate target offering amount for § 227.201(t) with interp, issuer and offering is at most the first-time issuer reviewed ceiling then financial statements reviewed by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer otherwise financial statements audited by a public accountant that is independent of the issuer.

<!-- l4: decide:an issuer may voluntarily meet the requirements for a higher aggregate target offering amount -->

**143.** An issuer may voluntarily meet the requirements for a higher aggregate target offering amount if—

    (a) An issuer may voluntarily meet the requirements of this paragraph (t) for a higher aggregate target offering amount.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the hundred and twentieth day, rolled off a weekend -->

**144.** In relation to a DATE “the end of the most recently completed fiscal year”, the hundred and twentieth day, rolled off a weekend means rolled forward off a weekend with Date with the sum of Day with the end of the most recently completed fiscal year and the financial statement staleness window in days.

<!-- l4: decide:the offering is conducted in the first 120 days of the fiscal year -->

**145.** In relation to a DATE “the end of the most recently completed fiscal year” and a DATE “the date of the offering”, the offering is conducted in the first 120 days of the fiscal year means the date of the offering is at most the hundred and twentieth day, rolled off a weekend with the end of the most recently completed fiscal year.

<!-- l4: decide:the failure to disclose a pre-2016 matter does not defeat the exemption -->

**146.** In relation to an IssuerProfile “issuer”, the failure to disclose a pre-2016 matter does not defeat the exemption if—

    (a) issuer's matters that would have triggered disqualification under § 227.503(a) but occurred before May 16, 2016;

    (b) it is not the case that issuer's those matters disclosed; and

    (c) issuer's did not know and, in the exercise of reasonable care, could not have known of the existence of the undisclosed matter.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's § 227.201 disclosure duty -->

**147.** The issuer must file with the Commission and provide to investors and the relevant intermediary the information required by § 227.201, provided that the offering statement discloses the information required by § 227.201 with offering. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.201: the offering statement does not disclose everything the section requires.

