    (i) (e);

    (j) offering's the disclosure provided's the current number of employees of the issuer;

    (k) (f);

    (l) offering's the disclosure provided's a discussion of the material factors that make an investment in the issuer speculative or risky;

    (m) (m);

    (n) offering's the disclosure provided's a description of the ownership and capital structure of the issuer;

    (o) (p);

    (p) offering's the disclosure provided's a description of the material terms of any indebtedness of the issuer;

    (q) (q);

    (r) offering's the disclosure provided's a description of exempt offerings conducted within the past three years;

    (s) (r);

    (t) offering's the disclosure provided's a description of related-party transactions above the five percent threshold;

    (u) (x);

    (v) offering's the disclosure provided's whether the issuer or any of its predecessors previously failed to comply with § 227.202;

    (w) (s); and

    (x) offering's the disclosure provided's a discussion of the issuer's financial condition.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's annual report duty -->

**149.** The issuer must file with the Commission and post on the issuer's Web site an annual report, provided that the annual report carries the disclosure § 227.202(a) requires with offering, within the annual report deadline in days. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.202(a): the annual report was not filed within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year, or does not carry the required disclosure.

<!-- l4: decide:the count of record holders for § 227.202(b)(2) -->

**150.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an IssuerProfile “issuer”, the count of record holders for § 227.202(b)(2) means consider the case distinctions of interp's holders of record basis :  when the investors who invested in the offering has  then issuer's investors who invested in the offering. when the register of holders of record has  then issuer's holders of record.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer may cease its ongoing reporting -->

**151.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an IssuerProfile “issuer”, the issuer may cease its ongoing reporting if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) (1); and

        (ii) issuer's required to file reports under section 13(a) or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act;

    (b) all of the following apply—

        (i) (2);

        (ii) issuer's annual reports filed since its most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part is at least 1; and

        (iii) the count of record holders for § 227.202(b)(2) with interp and issuer is less than the holders of record threshold;

    (c) all of the following apply—

        (i) (3);

        (ii) issuer's annual reports filed since its most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part is at least 3; and

        (iii) issuer's total assets is at most the total assets ceiling ending ongoing reporting;

    (d) all of the following apply—

        (i) (4); and

        (ii) issuer's all of the securities issued in reliance on section 4(a)(6) repurchased, including any payment in full of debt securities or any complete redemption of redeemable securities; or

    (e) all of the following apply—

        (i) (5); and

        (ii) issuer's liquidated or dissolved its business in accordance with state law.

## § 227.203 Filing requirements and form

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's offering statement filing duty -->

**152.** The issuer must file a Form C offering statement, provided that offering's the offering statement filed prior to the commencement of the offering and the offering statement discloses the information required by § 227.201 with offering. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.203(a)(1): Form C was not filed prior to the commencement of the offering, or does not include the information required by § 227.201.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's offering statement amendment duty -->

**153.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, the issuer's offering statement amendment duty means if offering's a material change to the terms of the offering or to the information provided by the issuer, then the issuer must file a Form C/A amendment to the offering statement. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.203(a)(2): no Form C/A was filed to disclose a material change.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's progress update duty -->

**154.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the issuer's progress update duty means if (iii) and intermediary's makes publicly available on its platform frequent updates regarding the progress of the issuer in meeting the target offering amount, then FULFILLED; otherwise, the issuer must file a Form C-U progress update, within five business days. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.203(a)(3)(i): no Form C-U was filed within five business days of reaching 50 percent or 100 percent of the target offering amount..

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's final progress update duty -->

**155.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, the issuer's final progress update duty means if offering's the issuer will accept investments in excess of the target offering amount, then the issuer must file a final Form C-U disclosing the total amount of securities sold, within five business days. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.203(a)(3)(ii): no final Form C-U was filed within five business days after the offering deadline.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

<!-- l4: decide:the instruction on consolidating progress updates -->

**156.** The instruction on consolidating progress updates if—

    (a) If multiple Forms C-U are triggered within the same five business day period, the issuer may consolidate such progress updates into one Form C-U, so long as the Form C-U discloses the most recent threshold that was met and the Form C-U is filed with the Commission and provided to investors and the relevant intermediary by the day on which the first progress update is due.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's Form C-AR duty -->

**157.** The issuer must file a Form C-AR annual report, within the annual report deadline in days. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.203(b)(1): Form C-AR was not filed within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's Form C-AR amendment duty -->

**158.** The issuer must file a Form C-AR/A amendment to the annual report, within five business days. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.203(b)(2): no Form C-AR/A was filed as soon as practicable after discovery of the need for a material change.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's termination of reporting duty -->

**159.** In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an IssuerProfile “issuer”, the issuer's termination of reporting duty means if the issuer may cease its ongoing reporting with interp and issuer, then the issuer must file a Form C-TR termination of reporting, within five business days. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.203(b)(3): Form C-TR was not filed within five business days of becoming eligible to terminate the reporting obligation.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

## § 227.206 Solicitations of interest and other communications

<!-- l4: decide:the solicitation of interest carries the statements § 227.206(b) requires -->

**160.** In relation to a Communication “communication”, the solicitation of interest carries the statements § 227.206(b) requires if—

    (a) (1);

    (b) communication's states that no money or other consideration is being solicited, and if sent in response, will not be accepted;

    (c) (2);

    (d) communication's states that no offer to buy the securities can be accepted and no part of the purchase price can be received until the offering statement is filed and only through an intermediary's platform;

    (e) (3); and

    (f) communication's states that a person's indication of interest involves no obligation or commitment of any kind.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's permission to solicit interest before filing -->

**161.** The issuer may communicate to determine whether there is any interest in a contemplated securities offering, provided that communication's made before the filing of the offering statement and the solicitation of interest carries the statements § 227.206(b) requires with communication.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer must not take money before the offering statement is filed -->

**162.** The issuer must not solicit or accept money, other consideration, or a commitment. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.206(a): money, other consideration or a commitment was solicited or accepted before the offering statement was filed.

<!-- l4: decide:the character and permitted response content of a solicitation of interest -->

**163.** The character and permitted response content of a solicitation of interest if—

    (a) Such communications are deemed to be an offer of a security for sale for purposes of the antifraud provisions of the Federal securities laws.;

    (b) This issuer may require the name, address, telephone number, and/or email address in any response form included pursuant to this paragraph (c).; and

    (c) TRUE.

## § 227.204 Advertising

<!-- l4: decide:the information a notice may contain under § 227.204(b) -->

**164.** The information a notice may contain under § 227.204(b) if—

    (a) (1) A statement that the issuer is conducting an offering pursuant to section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act, the name of the intermediary through which the offering is being conducted, and information (including a link in any written communications) directing the potential investor to the intermediary's platform;;

    (b) (2) The terms of the offering; and;

    (c) (3) Factual information about the legal identity and business location of the issuer, limited to the name of the issuer of the security, the address, phone number and Web site of the issuer, the email address of a representative of the issuer and a brief description of the business of the issuer.; and

    (d) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the notice qualifies under § 227.204(b) -->

**165.** In relation to a Communication “communication”, the notice qualifies under § 227.204(b) if—

    (a) communication's directs investors to the intermediary's platform; and

    (b) communication's includes no more than the information specified in § 227.204(b)(1) through (3).

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer must not advertise the terms of the offering -->

**166.** In relation to a Communication “communication”, the issuer must not advertise the terms of the offering means if the notice qualifies under § 227.204(b) with communication or the solicitation of interest carries the statements § 227.206(b) requires with communication, then FULFILLED; otherwise, the issuer must not advertise the terms of the offering. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.204(a)(1): the terms of the offering were advertised otherwise than by a notice meeting § 227.204(b) or a communication meeting § 227.206..

<!-- l4: decide:the meaning of "issuer" in § 227.204(a) -->

**167.** The meaning of "issuer" in § 227.204(a) if—

    (a) For purposes of this paragraph (a), issuer includes persons acting on behalf of the issuer.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's permission to use the intermediary's communication channels -->

**168.** The issuer may communicate with investors through the intermediary's communication channels, provided that communication's made through communication channels provided by an intermediary on the intermediary's platform and communication's the issuer identifies itself as the issuer in the communication and communication's a person acting on behalf of the issuer identifies that affiliation in the communication.

<!-- l4: decide:the concurrent-offering safe harbour in § 227.204(d) -->

**169.** The concurrent-offering safe harbour in § 227.204(d) if—

    (a) an issuer conducting an offering in reliance on Regulation Crowdfunding concurrently with another offering that discloses the terms of the Regulation Crowdfunding offering in the disclosure document for the other offering will not be deemed to have exceeded these disclosure limitations if the disclosure document for the other offering satisfies all the other requirements of this section.;

    (b) If the disclosure document for the other offering is filed on the Commission's Electronic Data Gathering and Retrieval System (EDGAR), the link required by paragraph (b)(1) may not be a live hyperlink.; and

    (c) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the meaning of "terms of the offering" -->

**170.** The meaning of "terms of the offering" if—

    (a) For purposes of this section, terms of the offering means the amount of securities offered, the nature of the securities, the price of the securities, the closing date of the offering period, the planned use of proceeds and the issuer's progress toward meeting its funding target.; and

    (b) TRUE.

## § 227.205 Promoter compensation

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's permission to compensate a promoter -->

**171.** The issuer may compensate a person to promote the issuer's offerings, provided that communication's made through communication channels provided by an intermediary on the intermediary's platform and communication's clearly discloses the receipt, past or prospective, of compensation with the communication.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer must not otherwise compensate a promoter -->

**172.** In relation to a Communication “communication”, the issuer must not otherwise compensate a promoter means if communication's made through communication channels provided by an intermediary on the intermediary's platform and communication's clearly discloses the receipt, past or prospective, of compensation with the communication or the notice qualifies under § 227.204(b) with communication, then FULFILLED; otherwise, the issuer must not compensate a person to promote the issuer's offerings. Failing which, breach by the issuer because § 227.205(b): a promoter was compensated otherwise than under § 227.205(a) or by a notice permitted by § 227.204..

## § 227.300 Intermediaries

<!-- l4: decide:the person qualifies to act as an intermediary -->

**173.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the person qualifies to act as an intermediary if—

    (a) (1);

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) intermediary's registered with the Commission as a broker under section 15(b) of the Exchange Act; or

        (ii) intermediary's registered as a funding portal in accordance with § 227.400;

    (c) (2); and

    (d) intermediary's a member of a national securities association registered under section 15A of the Exchange Act.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary's financial interest is permitted -->

**174.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary's financial interest is permitted if—

    (a) (1);

    (b) intermediary's that financial interest received from the issuer as compensation for the services provided in connection with the offer or sale;

    (c) (2); and

    (d) intermediary's that financial interest consists of securities of the same class and having the same terms, conditions and rights as the securities being offered.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary's financial interests comply with § 227.300(b) -->

**175.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary's financial interests comply with § 227.300(b) if—

    (a) intermediary's a director, officer or partner of the intermediary does not have a financial interest in the issuer; and

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) intermediary's the intermediary does not have a financial interest in the issuer; or

        (ii) the intermediary's financial interest is permitted with intermediary.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary is a funding portal -->

**176.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary is a funding portal if—

    (a) it is not the case that—

        (i) (i); and

        (ii) intermediary's offers investment advice or recommendations;

    (b) it is not the case that—

        (i) (ii); and

        (ii) intermediary's solicits purchases, sales or offers to buy the securities displayed on its platform;

    (c) it is not the case that—

        (i) (iii); and

        (ii) intermediary's compensates employees, agents, or other persons for such solicitation or based on the sale of securities displayed or referenced on its platform; and

    (d) it is not the case that—

        (i) (iv); and

        (ii) intermediary's holds, manages, possesses, or otherwise handles investor funds or securities.

<!-- l4: decide:the definitions in § 227.300(c) -->

**177.** The definitions in § 227.300(c) if—

    (a) (1) Associated person of a funding portal or person associated with a funding portal means any partner, officer, director or manager of a funding portal (or any person occupying a similar status or performing similar functions), any person directly or indirectly controlling or controlled by such funding portal, or any employee of a funding portal, except that any person associated with a funding portal whose functions are solely clerical or ministerial shall not be included in the meaning of such term for purposes of section 15(b) of the Exchange Act (other than paragraphs (4) and (6) of section 15(b) of the Exchange Act).;

    (b) (3) Intermediary means a broker registered under section 15(b) of the Exchange Act or a funding portal registered under § 227.400 and includes, where relevant, an associated person of the registered broker or registered funding portal.;

    (c) (4) Platform means a program or application accessible via the Internet or other similar electronic communication medium through which a registered broker or a registered funding portal acts as an intermediary in a transaction involving the offer or sale of securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act.;

    (d) An intermediary through which a crowdfunding transaction is conducted may engage in back office or other administrative functions other than on the intermediary's platform.; and

    (e) TRUE.

## § 227.302 Account opening

<!-- l4: declare:Educational materials -->

**178.** In this Act, “Educational materials” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “the process for the offer, purchase and issuance of securities through the intermediary and the risks associated with purchasing securities under section 4(a)(6)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “the types of securities available for purchase on the platform and the risks associated with each type, including the risk of having limited voting power as a result of dilution”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “the restrictions on the resale of a security offered and sold under section 4(a)(6)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “the types of information an issuer is required to provide under § 227.202, the frequency of delivery and the possibility that those obligations may terminate”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “the limitations on the amounts an investor may invest pursuant to § 227.100(a)(2)”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “the limitations on an investor's right to cancel an investment commitment and the circumstances in which a commitment may be cancelled by the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “the need for the investor to consider whether investing in such a security is appropriate for that investor”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “that following completion of an offering there may or may not be any ongoing relationship between the issuer and intermediary”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “that under certain circumstances an issuer may cease to publish annual reports and an investor may not continually have current financial information”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (j) “explained in plain language and otherwise designed to communicate effectively and accurately”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: decide:the educational materials carry everything § 227.302(b)(1) requires -->

**179.** In relation to an Educational materials “materials”, the educational materials carry everything § 227.302(b)(1) requires if—

    (a) (i);

    (b) materials's the process for the offer, purchase and issuance of securities through the intermediary and the risks associated with purchasing securities under section 4(a)(6);

    (c) (ii);

    (d) materials's the types of securities available for purchase on the platform and the risks associated with each type, including the risk of having limited voting power as a result of dilution;

    (e) (iii);

    (f) materials's the restrictions on the resale of a security offered and sold under section 4(a)(6);

    (g) (iv);

    (h) materials's the types of information an issuer is required to provide under § 227.202, the frequency of delivery and the possibility that those obligations may terminate;

    (i) (v);

    (j) materials's the limitations on the amounts an investor may invest pursuant to § 227.100(a)(2);

    (k) (vi);

    (l) materials's the limitations on an investor's right to cancel an investment commitment and the circumstances in which a commitment may be cancelled by the issuer;

    (m) (vii);

    (n) materials's the need for the investor to consider whether investing in such a security is appropriate for that investor;

    (o) (viii);

    (p) materials's that following completion of an offering there may or may not be any ongoing relationship between the issuer and intermediary;

    (q) (ix);

    (r) materials's that under certain circumstances an issuer may cease to publish annual reports and an investor may not continually have current financial information; and

    (s) materials's explained in plain language and otherwise designed to communicate effectively and accurately.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary must not accept a commitment before the account is opened -->

**180.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary must not accept a commitment before the account is opened means if intermediary's the investor has opened an account with the intermediary and intermediary's the intermediary has obtained from the investor consent to electronic delivery of materials, then FULFILLED; otherwise, the intermediary must not accept an investment commitment. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.302(a)(1): an investment commitment was accepted before the investor opened an account and consented to electronic delivery..

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary's educational materials duty -->

**181.** The intermediary must deliver the educational materials to the investor, provided that the educational materials carry everything § 227.302(b)(1) requires with materials. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.302(b)(1): the educational materials were not delivered, or do not explain in plain language everything the paragraph requires.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary complies with the rest of § 227.302 -->

**182.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary complies with the rest of § 227.302 if—

    (a) (a)(2);

    (b) intermediary's all subpart C information provided through electronic means;

    (c) (b)(2);

    (d) intermediary's the most current version of the educational materials available on its platform at all times;

    (e) (b)(2);

    (f) any of the following applies—

        (i) it is not the case that intermediary's a material revision made to the educational materials; or

        (ii) intermediary's the revised educational materials made available to all investors before accepting any additional investment commitments;

    (g) (c);

    (h) intermediary's the investor informed about the promoter disclosure requirement;

    (i) (d); and

    (j) intermediary's the manner in which the intermediary is compensated clearly disclosed.

## § 227.304 Completion of offerings, cancellations and reconfirmations

<!-- l4: decide:the investor may still cancel for any reason -->

**183.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering” and a DATE “the moment of cancellation”, the investor may still cancel for any reason means Day with the moment of cancellation is less than the difference between the result of dividing the cancellation cut-off in hours by 24 and Day with offering's deadline identified in the issuer's offering materials.

<!-- l4: decide:304(b)(1) — the offering remained open for at least 21 days -->

**184.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, 304(b)(1) — the offering remained open for at least 21 days if—

    (a) (1); and

    (b) the difference between Day with offering's date the § 227.201 and § 227.203(a) information was first made publicly available on the intermediary's platform and Day with offering's new offering deadline is at least the minimum public availability in days.

<!-- l4: decide:304(b)(2) — the early-close notice says what it must -->

**185.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, 304(b)(2) — the early-close notice says what it must if—

    (a) (i);

    (b) offering's notice given of the new, anticipated deadline of the offering;

    (c) (ii);

    (d) offering's notice given of the right of investors to cancel investment commitments for any reason until 48 hours prior to the new offering deadline;

    (e) (iii); and

    (f) offering's notice given of whether the issuer will continue to accept investment commitments during the 48-hour period prior to the new offering deadline.

<!-- l4: decide:304(b)(3) — the new deadline is at least five business days after the notice -->

**186.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, 304(b)(3) — the new deadline is at least five business days after the notice if—

    (a) (3); and

    (b) offering's new offering deadline is at least business days after with offering's date the notice of the new offering deadline was provided and five business days.

<!-- l4: decide:304(b)(4) — the target is still met at the new deadline -->

**187.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, 304(b)(4) — the target is still met at the new deadline if—

    (a) (4); and

    (b) offering's sum of the investment commitments is at least offering's target offering amount.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer may close the offering early -->

**188.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, the issuer may close the offering early if—

    (a) offering's sum of the investment commitments is at least offering's target offering amount;

    (b) offering's new offering deadline is less than offering's deadline identified in the issuer's offering materials;

    (c) 304(b)(1) — the offering remained open for at least 21 days with offering;

    (d) 304(b)(2) — the early-close notice says what it must with offering;

    (e) 304(b)(3) — the new deadline is at least five business days after the notice with offering; and

    (f) 304(b)(4) — the target is still met at the new deadline with offering.

<!-- l4: decide:the material change reconfirmation chain -->

**189.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering” and a CommitmentProfile “commitment”, the material change reconfirmation chain means if offering's a material change to the terms of the offering or to the information provided by the issuer, then the intermediary must give or send the investor notice of the material change, within five business days. Upon compliance, the investor must reconfirm the investment commitment, provided that commitment's reconfirmed within five business days of receipt of the notice, within five business days. Failing which, the intermediary must give or send the investor notice of the cancellation and the refund amount, within five business days. Upon compliance, the intermediary must direct the refund of investor funds, within five business days. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.304(c)(1)(ii): the refund of investor funds was not directed within five business days of the failure to reconfirm.. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.304(c)(1)(i): the investor was not notified of the cancellation, its reason and the refund amount within five business days of the failure to reconfirm... Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.304(c)(1): the investor was not given notice of the material change.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

<!-- l4: decide:the extension required by § 227.304(c)(2) -->

**190.** The extension required by § 227.304(c)(2) if—

    (a) If material changes to the offering or to the information provided by the issuer regarding the offering occur within five business days of the maximum number of days that an offering is to remain open, the offering must be extended to allow for a period of five business days for the investor to reconfirm his or her investment.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary's duties when the offering is not completed -->

**191.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, the intermediary's duties when the offering is not completed means if offering's the offering completed, then FULFILLED; otherwise, party the intermediary must give or send the investor notice of the cancellation and the refund amount has  within five business days hence FULFILLED lest breach by the intermediary because § 227.304(d)(1): each investor was not notified of the cancellation, its reason and the refund amount within five business days and party the intermediary must direct the refund of investor funds has  within five business days hence FULFILLED lest breach by the intermediary because § 227.304(d)(2): the refund of investor funds was not directed within five business days and party the intermediary must prevent investors from making investment commitments with respect to that offering has  within five business days hence FULFILLED lest breach by the intermediary because § 227.304(d)(3): investors were not prevented from making further investment commitments within five business days.

## § 227.303 Requirements with respect to transactions

<!-- l4: declare:Commitment notice -->

**192.** In this Act, “Commitment notice” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “the dollar amount of the investment commitment”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “the price of the securities, if known”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “the name of the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (d) “the date and time by which the investor may cancel the investment commitment”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:Transaction confirmation -->

**193.** In this Act, “Transaction confirmation” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “the date of the transaction”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “the type of security that the investor is purchasing”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “the identity, price, and number of securities purchased by the investor, the number sold by the issuer and the prices at which they were sold”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “if a debt security, the interest rate and the yield to maturity calculated from the price paid and the maturity date”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “if a callable security, the first date that the security can be called by the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (f) “the source, form and amount of any remuneration received or to be received by the intermediary in connection with the transaction”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: declare:qualified third party -->

**194.** In this Act, “qualified third party” means one of the following—

    (a) “a registered broker or dealer that carries customer or broker or dealer accounts and holds funds or securities for those persons”; or

    (b) “a bank or credit union insured by the National Credit Union Administration that has agreed in writing to hold the funds in escrow or to maintain an account for the exclusive benefit of investors and the issuer”.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary has made the issuer information publicly available as § 227.303(a) requires -->

**195.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, an OfferingProfile “offering” and a DATE “the date of the first sale”, the intermediary has made the issuer information publicly available as § 227.303(a) requires if—

    (a) (1);

    (b) intermediary's the issuer information made publicly available on its platform in a manner that reasonably permits a person to save, download, or otherwise store it;

    (c) (2);

    (d) the difference between Day with offering's date the § 227.201 and § 227.203(a) information was first made publicly available on the intermediary's platform and Day with the date of the first sale is at least the minimum public availability in days;

    (e) (3);

    (f) intermediary's the issuer information remains publicly available until the offer and sale is completed or cancelled;

    (g) (4); and

    (h) intermediary's no person required to establish an account with the intermediary to access that information.

<!-- l4: decide:the questionnaire demonstrates what § 227.303(b)(2)(ii) requires -->

**196.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the questionnaire demonstrates what § 227.303(b)(2)(ii) requires if—

    (a) (A);

    (b) intermediary's a questionnaire obtained demonstrating the investor's understanding of the restrictions on cancellation;

    (c) (B);

    (d) intermediary's a questionnaire obtained demonstrating the investor's understanding that it may be difficult to resell the securities;

    (e) (C); and

    (f) intermediary's a questionnaire obtained demonstrating the investor's understanding that investing involves risk and that he or she should not invest funds he or she cannot afford to lose.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary has qualified the investor as § 227.303(b) requires -->

**197.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary has qualified the investor as § 227.303(b) requires if—

    (a) (1);

    (b) intermediary's a reasonable basis for believing that the investor satisfies the investment limitations;

    (c) (2)(i);

    (d) intermediary's a representation obtained that the investor has reviewed the educational materials, understands that the entire investment may be lost, and is in a financial condition to bear the loss;

    (e) (2)(ii); and

    (f) the questionnaire demonstrates what § 227.303(b)(2)(ii) requires with intermediary.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary's communication channels comply with § 227.303(c) -->

**198.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary's communication channels comply with § 227.303(c) if—

    (a) intermediary's communication channels provided on its platform;

    (b) (1);

    (c) any of the following applies—

        (i) the intermediary is not a funding portal with intermediary; or

        (ii) intermediary's it does not participate in those communications other than to establish guidelines and remove abusive or potentially fraudulent communications;

    (d) (2);

    (e) intermediary's public access permitted to view the discussions in the communication channels;

    (f) (3);

    (g) intermediary's posting of comments restricted to persons who have opened an account;

    (h) (4); and

    (i) intermediary's each person posting a comment required to disclose any promotional relationship with the issuer.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary's notice-of-commitment duty -->

**199.** The intermediary must give or send the investor notice of the investment commitment, provided that (1) and notice's the dollar amount of the investment commitment and (2) and notice's the price of the securities, if known and (3) and notice's the name of the issuer and (4) and notice's the date and time by which the investor may cancel the investment commitment. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.303(d): the investor was not promptly given a notification disclosing the amount, the price, the issuer and the cancellation deadline.

<!-- l4: decide:the maintenance and transmission of funds under § 227.303(e)(1)-(2) -->

**200.** The maintenance and transmission of funds under § 227.303(e)(1)-(2) if—

    (a) (1) An intermediary that is a registered broker must comply with the requirements of 17 CFR 240.15c2-4.;

    (b) (2) An intermediary that is a funding portal must direct investors to transmit the money or other consideration directly to a qualified third party that has agreed in writing to hold the funds for the benefit of, and to promptly transmit or return the funds to, the persons entitled thereto in accordance with paragraph (e)(3) of this section.; and

    (c) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the funding portal may direct the transmission of funds to the issuer -->

**201.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering” and a DATE “the date of the proposed transmission”, the funding portal may direct the transmission of funds to the issuer if—

    (a) offering's sum of the investment commitments is at least offering's target offering amount;

    (b) it is not the case that the investor may still cancel for any reason with offering and the date of the proposed transmission; and

    (c) the difference between Day with offering's date the § 227.201 and § 227.203(a) information was first made publicly available on the intermediary's platform and Day with the date of the proposed transmission is at least the minimum public availability in days.

<!-- l4: decide:the funding portal's fund-flow duty -->

**202.** In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering” and a DATE “the date of the proposed transmission”, the funding portal's fund-flow duty means if the funding portal may direct the transmission of funds to the issuer with offering and the date of the proposed transmission, then the funding portal may direct the qualified third party to transmit the funds to the issuer.; otherwise, the funding portal must direct the refund of investor funds. Failing which, breach by the funding portal because § 227.303(e)(3)(ii)-(iii): funds were neither transmitted lawfully nor returned to investors on cancellation or on failure to complete the offering..

<!-- l4: decide:the confirmation discloses everything § 227.303(f)(1) requires -->

**203.** In relation to a Transaction confirmation “confirmation”, the confirmation discloses everything § 227.303(f)(1) requires if—

    (a) (i);

    (b) confirmation's the date of the transaction;

    (c) (ii);

    (d) confirmation's the type of security that the investor is purchasing;

    (e) (iii);

    (f) confirmation's the identity, price, and number of securities purchased by the investor, the number sold by the issuer and the prices at which they were sold;

    (g) (iv);

    (h) confirmation's if a debt security, the interest rate and the yield to maturity calculated from the price paid and the maturity date;

    (i) (v);

    (j) confirmation's if a callable security, the first date that the security can be called by the issuer;

    (k) (vi); and

    (l) confirmation's the source, form and amount of any remuneration received or to be received by the intermediary in connection with the transaction.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary's transaction confirmation duty -->

**204.** The intermediary must give or send the investor confirmation of the transaction, provided that the confirmation discloses everything § 227.303(f)(1) requires with confirmation. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.303(f)(1): the investor was not given a notification disclosing all six required items at or before the completion of the transaction.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary is exempt from § 240.10b-10 for this transaction -->

**205.** In relation to a Transaction confirmation “confirmation”, the intermediary is exempt from § 240.10b-10 for this transaction means the confirmation discloses everything § 227.303(f)(1) requires with confirmation.

## § 227.301 Measures to reduce risk of fraud

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary has the reasonable bases § 227.301(a)-(b) requires -->

**206.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary has the reasonable bases § 227.301(a)-(b) requires if—

    (a) (a);

    (b) intermediary's a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer complies with section 4A(b) of the Securities Act and the related requirements in this part;

    (c) (b); and

    (d) any of the following applies—

        (i) intermediary's a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer has established means to keep accurate records of the holders of the securities; or

        (ii) intermediary's the issuer has engaged the services of a transfer agent registered under section 17A of the Exchange Act.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary's duty to deny access for a disqualification -->

**207.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary's duty to deny access for a disqualification means if (1) and intermediary's a reasonable basis for believing that a covered person is subject to a disqualification under § 227.503, then the intermediary must deny access to its platform to the issuer, provided that intermediary's a background and securities enforcement regulatory history check conducted on the issuer and on each officer, director and twenty percent beneficial owner. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.301(c)(1): access was not denied to an issuer reasonably believed to be subject to a § 227.503 disqualification, or the minimum background and regulatory-history check was not conducted.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary's duty on a fraud or investor-protection concern -->

**208.** In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the intermediary's duty on a fraud or investor-protection concern means if (2) and intermediary's a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer or the offering presents the potential for fraud or otherwise raises concerns about investor protection or intermediary's unable to adequately or effectively assess the risk of fraud of the issuer or its potential offering, then if intermediary's became aware of that information after granting access, then the intermediary must remove the offering from its platform, cancel the offering, and return the funds committed by investors. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.301(c)(2): on becoming aware after granting access, the offering was not promptly removed and cancelled and the committed funds were not returned.; otherwise, the intermediary must deny access to its platform to the issuer. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.301(c)(2): access was not denied although the issuer or the offering presents the potential for fraud or raises concerns about investor protection.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

## § 227.305 Payments to third parties

<!-- l4: decide:the intermediary must not pay for investor personal information -->

**209.** The intermediary must not compensate a person for the personally identifiable information of an investor. Failing which, breach by the intermediary because § 227.305(a): a person was compensated for providing the personally identifiable information of an investor or potential investor.

<!-- l4: decide:the meaning of "personally identifiable information" -->

**210.** The meaning of "personally identifiable information" if—

    (a) For purposes of this rule, personally identifiable information means information that can be used to distinguish or trace an individual's identity, either alone or when combined with other personal or identifying information that is linked or linkable to a specific individual.; and

    (b) TRUE.

## § 227.400 Registration of funding portals

<!-- l4: decide:the date the funding portal's registration becomes effective -->

**211.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the date the funding portal's registration becomes effective means if Day with thirty calendar days after receipt is at least Day with portal's date approved for membership by a registered national securities association, then thirty calendar days after receipt; otherwise, portal's date approved for membership by a registered national securities association.

For the purposes of this provision—

“thirty calendar days after receipt” means Date with the sum of Day with portal's date the registration was received by the Commission and the portal registration effectiveness in days;

<!-- l4: decide:the funding portal's registration duty -->

**212.** The funding portal must register on Form Funding Portal and become a member of a national securities association, provided that portal's a complete Form Funding Portal filed with the Commission. Failing which, breach by the funding portal because § 227.400(a): a complete Form Funding Portal was not filed with the Commission, or the portal did not become a member of a registered national securities association.

<!-- l4: decide:the funding portal's amendment duty -->

**213.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the funding portal's amendment duty means if portal's information previously submitted on Form Funding Portal has become inaccurate, then the funding portal must file an amendment to Form Funding Portal, within the portal amendment window in days. Failing which, breach by the funding portal because § 227.400(b): no amendment to Form Funding Portal was filed within 30 days of the information becoming inaccurate.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

<!-- l4: decide:the date the predecessor's registration is deemed withdrawn -->

**214.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the date the predecessor's registration is deemed withdrawn means Date with the sum of Day with portal's date the successor filed a registration on Form Funding Portal and the predecessor deemed withdrawal in days.

<!-- l4: decide:the predecessor's registration remains effective as the successor's -->

**215.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the predecessor's registration remains effective as the successor's if—

    (a) portal's succeeds to and continues the business of a registered funding portal; and

    (b) the difference between Day with portal's date of the succession and Day with portal's date the successor filed a registration on Form Funding Portal is at most the portal amendment window in days.

<!-- l4: decide:the pure-form succession alternative in § 227.400(c)(2) -->

**216.** The pure-form succession alternative in § 227.400(c)(2) if—

    (a) if a funding portal succeeds to and continues the business of a registered funding portal and the succession is based solely on a change of the predecessor's date or state of incorporation, form of organization, or composition of a partnership, the successor may, within 30 days after the succession, amend the registration of the predecessor on Form Funding Portal to reflect these changes.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the date the withdrawal becomes effective -->

**217.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the date the withdrawal becomes effective means if Day with thirty days after receipt of the withdrawal is at least Day with portal's a longer period consented to by the funding portal or determined by the Commission by order, then thirty days after receipt of the withdrawal; otherwise, portal's a longer period consented to by the funding portal or determined by the Commission by order.

For the purposes of this provision—

“thirty days after receipt of the withdrawal” means Date with the sum of Day with portal's date the withdrawal was received by the Commission and the portal registration effectiveness in days;

<!-- l4: decide:the funding portal's withdrawal duty -->

**218.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the funding portal's withdrawal duty means if portal's has ceased to operate as a funding portal, then the funding portal must file a withdrawal of registration on Form Funding Portal. Failing which, breach by the funding portal because § 227.400(d): a withdrawal of registration was not promptly filed on ceasing to operate as a funding portal.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

<!-- l4: decide:when a Form Funding Portal is filed, and the duplicate originals -->

**219.** When a Form Funding Portal is filed, and the duplicate originals if—

    (a) The applications and reports provided for in this section shall be considered filed when a complete Form Funding Portal is submitted with the Commission.;

    (b) Duplicate originals of the applications and reports provided for in this section must be filed with surveillance personnel designated by any registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member.; and

    (c) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the nonresident information-sharing condition is met -->

**220.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the nonresident information-sharing condition is met if—

    (a) it is not the case that portal's nonresident; or

    (b) portal's an information sharing arrangement in place between the Commission and the competent regulator.

<!-- l4: decide:the meaning of "nonresident funding portal" -->

**221.** The meaning of "nonresident funding portal" if—

    (a) For purposes of this section, the term nonresident funding portal shall mean a funding portal incorporated in or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction outside of the United States or its territories, or having its principal place of business in any place not in the United States or its territories.; and

    (b) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the nonresident portal's power-of-attorney obligations are met -->

**222.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the nonresident portal's power-of-attorney obligations are met if—

    (a) (i);

    (b) portal's a written consent and power of attorney appointing an agent in the United States obtained;

    (c) (ii);

    (d) portal's the name and address of its United States agent for service of process furnished on Schedule C;

    (e) (iii);

    (f) portal's a change of agent communicated promptly to the Commission through amendment of Schedule C;

    (g) (iv);

    (h) portal's a successor agent for service of process promptly appointed where required;

    (i) (v); and

    (j) portal's the written consent and power of attorney maintained as part of its books and records for at least three years after termination.

<!-- l4: decide:the nonresident portal's books-and-records certification is in place -->

**223.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the nonresident portal's books-and-records certification is in place if—

    (a) (A);

    (b) portal's certified on Schedule C that it can and will provide prompt access to its books and records and submit to onsite inspection and examination;

    (c) (B); and

    (d) portal's an opinion of counsel provided that it can, as a matter of law, provide that access and submit to that inspection.

<!-- l4: decide:the nonresident portal's re-certification duty -->

**224.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the nonresident portal's re-certification duty means if portal's nonresident and portal's a change in the legal or regulatory framework affecting that access or inspection, then the funding portal must re-certify on Schedule C to Form Funding Portal, within the re-certification window in days. Failing which, breach by the funding portal because § 227.400(f)(3)(ii): the portal did not re-certify on Schedule C, with a revised opinion of counsel, within 90 days of the change in the legal or regulatory framework.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

## § 227.401 Exemption

<!-- l4: decide:the funding portal is exempt from broker registration under section 15(a)(1) -->

**225.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the funding portal is exempt from broker registration under section 15(a)(1) if—

    (a) A funding portal that is registered with the Commission pursuant to § 227.400 is exempt from the broker registration requirements of section 15(a)(1) of the Exchange Act in connection with its activities as a funding portal.; and

    (b) portal's a complete Form Funding Portal filed with the Commission.

## § 227.403 Compliance

<!-- l4: decide:the funding portal complies with § 227.403 -->

**226.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the funding portal complies with § 227.403 if—

    (a) (a);

    (b) portal's written policies and procedures reasonably designed to achieve compliance with the federal securities laws implemented;

    (c) (b);

    (d) portal's complies with the requirements of part 248 of this chapter as they apply to brokers;

    (e) (c); and

    (f) portal's permits the examination and inspection of its business and business operations.

## § 227.404 Records to be made and kept by funding portals

<!-- l4: decide:the governing retention period in years -->

**227.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the governing retention period in years means if portal's subject to the requirements of the Currency and Foreign Transactions Reporting Act of 1970, then max with the record retention in years and portal's the retention period required by 31 CFR chapter X in years; otherwise, the record retention in years.

<!-- l4: decide:the nine categories of records § 227.404(a) requires -->

**228.** The nine categories of records § 227.404(a) requires if—

    (a) (1) All records related to an investor who purchases or attempts to purchase securities through the funding portal;;

    (b) (2) All records related to issuers who offer and sell or attempt to offer and sell securities through the funding portal and the control persons of such issuers;;

    (c) (3) Records of all communications that occur on or through its platform;;

    (d) (4) All records related to persons that use communication channels provided by a funding portal to promote an issuer's securities or communicate with potential investors;;

    (e) (5) All records required to demonstrate compliance with the requirements of subparts C and D of this part;;

    (f) (6) All notices provided by such funding portal to issuers and investors generally through the funding portal's platform or otherwise;;

    (g) (7) All written agreements (or copies thereof) entered into by such funding portal relating to its business as such;;

    (h) (8) All daily, monthly and quarterly summaries of transactions effected through the funding portal;;

    (i) (9) A log reflecting the progress of each issuer who offers or sells securities through the funding portal toward meeting the target offering amount.; and

    (j) TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the funding portal's recordkeeping duty -->

**229.** In relation to a FundingPortalProfile “portal”, the funding portal's recordkeeping duty if—

    (a) party the funding portal must make and preserve the records required by § 227.404 has  provided that (a) and portal's the nine categories of records made and preserved for five years, the first two years in an easily accessible place and (b) and portal's organizational documents made and preserved during the operation of the funding portal and of any successor and (c) and portal's records produced, reproduced and maintained in the original, non-alterable format or as permitted under § 240.17a-4(f) and (d) and portal's a written undertaking filed with the registered national securities association where a third party maintains the records hence FULFILLED lest breach by the funding portal because § 227.404(a)-(d): the required records were not made, preserved for the governing period, kept in a non-alterable format, or covered by the required third-party undertaking; and

    (b) party the funding portal must permit the examination and inspection of its business and business operations has  provided that (e) and portal's records furnished promptly to the Commission and the association on request hence FULFILLED lest breach by the funding portal because § 227.404(e): records were not furnished promptly to the Commission or to the registered national securities association on request.

<!-- l4: decide:the third-party undertaking § 227.404(d) prescribes -->

**230.** The third-party undertaking § 227.404(d) prescribes if—

    (a) With respect to any books and records maintained or preserved on behalf of [name of funding portal], the undersigned hereby acknowledges that the books and records are the property of [name of funding portal], and hereby undertakes to permit examination of such books and records at any time, or from time to time, during business hours by representatives of the Securities and Exchange Commission and the registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member, and to promptly furnish to the Commission, its representatives, and the registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member, a true, correct, complete and current hard copy of any, all, or any part of, such books and records.; and

    (b) TRUE.

## § 227.402 Conditional safe harbor

<!-- l4: decide:the framing of the conditional safe harbor in § 227.402(a) -->

**231.** The framing of the conditional safe harbor in § 227.402(a) if—

    (a) Under section 3(a)(80) of the Exchange Act, a funding portal acting as an intermediary in a transaction involving the offer or sale of securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act may not: offer investment advice or recommendations; solicit purchases, sales, or offers to buy the securities offered or displayed on its platform or portal; compensate employees, agents, or other persons for such solicitation or based on the sale of securities displayed or referenced on its platform or portal; hold, manage, possess, or otherwise handle investor funds or securities; or engage in such other activities as the Commission, by rule, determines appropriate.;

    (b) No presumption shall arise that a funding portal has violated the prohibitions under section 3(a)(80) of the Exchange Act or this part by reason of the funding portal or its associated persons engaging in activities in connection with the offer or sale of securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act that do not meet the conditions specified in paragraph (b) of this section.;

    (c) The antifraud provisions and all other applicable provisions of the federal securities laws continue to apply to the activities described in paragraph (b) of this section.; and

    (d) TRUE.

<!-- l4: declare:funding portal activity -->

**232.** In this Act, “funding portal activity” means one of the following—

    (a) “determining whether and under what terms to allow an issuer to offer and sell securities through its platform”;

    (b) “applying objective criteria to highlight offerings on the platform”;

    (c) “providing search, sort or categorisation tools”;

    (d) “providing communication channels”;

    (e) “advising an issuer about the structure or content of the issuer's offering”;

    (f) “compensating a third party for referring a person to the funding portal”;

    (g) “paying compensation to a registered broker or dealer for services”;

    (h) “receiving compensation from a registered broker or dealer for services”;

    (i) “advertising the existence of the funding portal and identifying issuers or offerings on the basis of objective criteria”;

    (j) “denying access to the platform to, or cancelling an offering of, an issuer pursuant to § 227.301(c)(2)”;

    (k) “accepting, on behalf of an issuer, an investment commitment”;

    (l) “directing investors where to transmit funds or remit payment”; or

    (m) “directing a qualified third party to release proceeds to an issuer or to return proceeds to investors”.

<!-- l4: declare:Portal activity -->

**233.** In this Act, “Portal activity” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “the activity”, being a funding portal activity;

    (b) “the funding portal otherwise complies with this part”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “the criteria are reasonably designed to highlight or identify a broad selection of issuers, are applied consistently to all issuers and offerings, and are clearly displayed on the platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “the criteria do not include the advisability of investing in the issuer or its offering, or an assessment of any characteristic of the issuer, its business plan, its key management or the risks associated with an investment”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (e) “the funding portal does not receive special or additional compensation for highlighting or identifying one or more issuers or offerings”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (f) “it does not participate in the communications other than to establish guidelines for communication and remove abusive or potentially fraudulent communications”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (g) “public access permitted to view the discussions in the communication channels”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (h) “posting of comments restricted to persons who have opened an account on its platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (i) “each person posting a comment required to disclose any promotional relationship with the issuer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (j) “the third party does not provide the funding portal with personally identifiable information of any potential investor”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (k) “the referral compensation, other than that paid to a registered broker or dealer, is not based on the purchase or sale of a security offered on or through the platform”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (l) “the services are provided pursuant to a written agreement between the funding portal and the registered broker or dealer”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (m) “the services and compensation are permitted under this part”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (n) “the services and compensation comply with the rules of any registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (o) “a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer or the offering presents the potential for fraud or otherwise raises concerns about investor protection”, being a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: decide:the objective-criteria conditions are met -->

**234.** In relation to a Portal activity “activity”, the objective-criteria conditions are met if—

    (a) activity's the criteria are reasonably designed to highlight or identify a broad selection of issuers, are applied consistently to all issuers and offerings, and are clearly displayed on the platform;

    (b) activity's the criteria do not include the advisability of investing in the issuer or its offering, or an assessment of any characteristic of the issuer, its business plan, its key management or the risks associated with an investment; and

    (c) activity's the funding portal does not receive special or additional compensation for highlighting or identifying one or more issuers or offerings.

<!-- l4: decide:the communication-channel conditions are met -->

**235.** In relation to a Portal activity “activity”, the communication-channel conditions are met if—

    (a) (i);

    (b) activity's it does not participate in the communications other than to establish guidelines for communication and remove abusive or potentially fraudulent communications;

    (c) (ii);

    (d) activity's public access permitted to view the discussions in the communication channels;

    (e) (iii);

    (f) activity's posting of comments restricted to persons who have opened an account on its platform;

    (g) (iv); and

    (h) activity's each person posting a comment required to disclose any promotional relationship with the issuer.

<!-- l4: decide:the broker-dealer compensation conditions are met -->

**236.** In relation to a Portal activity “activity”, the broker-dealer compensation conditions are met if—

    (a) (i);

    (b) activity's the services are provided pursuant to a written agreement between the funding portal and the registered broker or dealer;

    (c) (ii);

    (d) activity's the services and compensation are permitted under this part;

    (e) (iii); and

    (f) activity's the services and compensation comply with the rules of any registered national securities association of which the funding portal is a member.

<!-- l4: decide:the activity falls within the funding portal safe harbour -->

**237.** In relation to a Portal activity “activity”, the activity falls within the funding portal safe harbour means consider the case distinctions of activity's the activity :  when determining whether and under what terms to allow an issuer to offer and sell securities through its platform has  then activity's the funding portal otherwise complies with this part. when applying objective criteria to highlight offerings on the platform has  then the objective-criteria conditions are met with activity. when providing search, sort or categorisation tools has  then activity's the criteria do not include the advisability of investing in the issuer or its offering, or an assessment of any characteristic of the issuer, its business plan, its key management or the risks associated with an investment. when providing communication channels has  then the communication-channel conditions are met with activity. when advising an issuer about the structure or content of the issuer's offering has  then TRUE. when compensating a third party for referring a person to the funding portal has  then activity's the third party does not provide the funding portal with personally identifiable information of any potential investor and activity's the referral compensation, other than that paid to a registered broker or dealer, is not based on the purchase or sale of a security offered on or through the platform. when paying compensation to a registered broker or dealer for services has  then the broker-dealer compensation conditions are met with activity. when receiving compensation from a registered broker or dealer for services has  then the broker-dealer compensation conditions are met with activity. when advertising the existence of the funding portal and identifying issuers or offerings on the basis of objective criteria has  then the objective-criteria conditions are met with activity. when denying access to the platform to, or cancelling an offering of, an issuer pursuant to § 227.301(c)(2) has  then activity's a reasonable basis for believing that the issuer or the offering presents the potential for fraud or otherwise raises concerns about investor protection. when accepting, on behalf of an issuer, an investment commitment has  then TRUE. when directing investors where to transmit funds or remit payment has  then TRUE. when directing a qualified third party to release proceeds to an issuer or to return proceeds to investors has  then TRUE.

## § 227.502 Insignificant deviations from a term, condition or requirement of this part

<!-- l4: decide:502(a)(3) — the issuer's knowledge limb -->

**238.** In relation to a DeviationClaim “claim”, 502(a)(3) — the issuer's knowledge limb if—

    (a) all of the following apply—

        (i) (3); and

        (ii) it is not the case that claim's the failure resulted from the intermediary's failure to comply with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act and the related rules;

    (b) claim's the issuer did not know of such failure; or

    (c) claim's the intermediary's failure occurred solely in offerings other than the issuer's offering.

<!-- l4: decide:the failure to comply does not cost the exemption for a particular purchaser -->

**239.** In relation to a DeviationClaim “claim”, the failure to comply does not cost the exemption for a particular purchaser if—

    (a) (1);

    (b) claim's the failure to comply was insignificant with respect to the offering as a whole;

    (c) (2);

    (d) claim's the issuer made a good faith and reasonable attempt to comply with all applicable terms, conditions and requirements of this part; and

    (e) 502(a)(3) — the issuer's knowledge limb with claim.

<!-- l4: decide:§ 227.502(b) preserves the Commission's enforcement powers -->

**240.** § 227.502(b) preserves the Commission's enforcement powers if—

    (a) Paragraph (a) of this section shall not preclude the Commission from bringing an enforcement action seeking any appropriate relief for an issuer's failure to comply with all applicable terms, conditions and requirements of this part.; and

    (b) TRUE.

## Entry points — the decisions a caller actually asks for

<!-- l4: decide:the exemption is available -->

**241. export Decide whether the Regulation Crowdfunding exemption under Securities Act section 4(a)(6) is available for a particular sale of securities by a particular issuer to a particular investor.**

In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an IssuerProfile “issuer”, an OfferingProfile “offering”, an InvestorProfile “investor”, a NUMBER “this investment” and a DATE “the date of the offer or sale”, the exemption is available means the crowdfunding exemption is available with interp, issuer, offering, investor, this investment and the date of the offer or sale.

<!-- l4: decide:the investment limit -->

**242. export Calculate the maximum dollar amount a particular investor may invest across all Regulation Crowdfunding issuers in a 12-month period, under 17 CFR 227.100(a)(2).**

In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an InvestorProfile “investor”, the investment limit means the investment limit for the investor with interp and investor.

<!-- l4: decide:the issuer's remaining capacity under the twelve month cap -->

**243. export Calculate how much more an issuer may raise under Regulation Crowdfunding before hitting the $5,000,000 rolling 12-month cap in 17 CFR 227.100(a)(1).**

In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an IssuerProfile “issuer”, an OfferingProfile “offering” and a DATE “the date of the offer or sale”, the issuer's remaining capacity under the twelve month cap means the issuer's headroom under the twelve month cap with interp, issuer, offering and the date of the offer or sale.

<!-- l4: decide:the financial statement level required -->

**244. export Determine which level of financial statements an issuer must provide with its Regulation Crowdfunding offering statement — tax return information, reviewed, or audited — under 17 CFR 227.201(t).**

In relation to an Interpretation “interp”, an IssuerProfile “issuer” and an OfferingProfile “offering”, the financial statement level required means the financial statements required with interp, issuer and offering.

<!-- l4: decide:the ongoing reporting obligation continues -->

**245. export Determine whether an issuer must keep filing Regulation Crowdfunding annual reports, or may stop, under 17 CFR 227.202(b).**

In relation to an Interpretation “interp” and an IssuerProfile “issuer”, the ongoing reporting obligation continues if it is not the case that the issuer may cease its ongoing reporting with interp and issuer.

<!-- l4: decide:the resale is permitted -->

**246. export Determine whether securities acquired in a Regulation Crowdfunding offering may lawfully be transferred, under the one-year resale restriction in 17 CFR 227.501.**

In relation to a Transfer “transfer”, the resale is permitted means the transfer is permitted with transfer.

<!-- l4: decide:the person is a disqualifying covered person -->

**247. export Determine whether a covered person's criminal, regulatory or administrative history disqualifies an issuer's Regulation Crowdfunding offering under 17 CFR 227.503(a).**

In relation to a CoveredPerson “person” and a DATE “the filing”, the person is a disqualifying covered person means the covered person is disqualified with person and the filing.

<!-- l4: decide:the offering may be closed early -->

**248. export Determine whether an issuer that has reached its target offering amount may close its Regulation Crowdfunding offering before the deadline in its offering materials, under 17 CFR 227.304(b).**

In relation to an OfferingProfile “offering”, the offering may be closed early means the issuer may close the offering early with offering.

<!-- l4: decide:the person may act as an intermediary -->

**249. export Determine whether a person is qualified to act as an intermediary in a Regulation Crowdfunding transaction, under 17 CFR 227.300(a).**

In relation to an IntermediaryProfile “intermediary”, the person may act as an intermediary means the person qualifies to act as an intermediary with intermediary.

<!-- l4: decide:the funding portal activity is within the safe harbour -->

**250. export Determine whether an activity a funding portal proposes to undertake falls within the conditional safe harbor in 17 CFR 227.402(b), so that it does not breach the Exchange Act section 3(a)(80) prohibitions.**

In relation to a Portal activity “activity”, the funding portal activity is within the safe harbour means the activity falls within the funding portal safe harbour with activity.

## Fixtures — constructors that vary one thing at a time

<!-- l4: decide:an investor -->

**251.** In relation to a STRING “who”, a BOOLEAN “natural”, a NUMBER “income”, a NUMBER “worth”, a NUMBER “revenue”, a NUMBER “assets” and a NUMBER “already invested”, an investor means InvestorProfile where name is who, a natural person is natural, within a category of § 230.501(a)(1)-(4) or (7)-(13) at the time of the sale, or reasonably believed to be is FALSE, annual income for the calendar year is income, annual income for the investor's own fiscal year is income, revenue for the most recent fiscal year is revenue, net assets as of the most recent fiscal year end is assets, total assets other than the primary residence is worth, total liabilities other than indebtedness secured by the primary residence is 0, estimated fair market value of the primary residence at the time of the sale is 0, indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding at the time of the sale is 0, indebtedness secured by the primary residence outstanding 60 days before the sale is 0, the increase in that indebtedness was the result of the acquisition of the primary residence is FALSE, the purchase is made in accordance with a right to purchase such securities is FALSE, that right was held by the person on July 20, 2010 is FALSE, qualified as an accredited investor on the basis of net worth at the time the right was acquired is FALSE, held securities of the same issuer, other than such right, on July 20, 2010 is FALSE, net worth calculated without the paragraph (a)(5)(i) adjustments is worth, individual income in each of the two most recent years is income, joint income with a spouse or spousal equivalent in each of those years is 0, a reasonable expectation of reaching the same income level in the current year is TRUE, aggregate amount of securities sold to the investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months is already invested, annual income and net worth calculated jointly with that person's spouse is FALSE and the aggregate investment of